WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:07.359 align:start position:0%
Hi, this is Matt Baker. Today's video is
a new compilation of all the various

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:12.160 align:start position:0%
videos we've done related to our world
religions family tree chart. Once again,

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:18.000 align:start position:0%
there are sections on Hinduism,
Buddhism, Chinese religions, Judaism,

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:22.320 align:start position:0%
and Islam. But this time, I've also
added the videos we've done about

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:27.359 align:start position:0%
Sikhism, Christianity, and Western
esotericism. If you want to get a copy

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:32.160 align:start position:0%
of the chart as a poster, just click on
the link in the description or pinned

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:36.160 align:start position:0%
comment or visit us anytime over at
usefulcharts.com.

00:00:34.239 --> 00:00:40.719 align:start position:0%
Before we dive into each section though,
let me tell you a few things about the

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:45.040 align:start position:0%
chart in general. So, first of all, you
can see here at the top that I've

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:48.879 align:start position:0%
included an infographic showing the
approximate number of followers in each

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:53.360 align:start position:0%
major religion so that you can get a
rough idea of how the world population

00:00:51.039 --> 00:00:58.079 align:start position:0%
breaks down. Now, regardless of which
data source one uses, I've used the one

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:02.239 align:start position:0%
from an organization called the Pew
Research Center, what every source

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.600 align:start position:0%
agrees on is that the four largest
religions in the world are in order

00:01:04.479 --> 00:01:14.560 align:start position:0%
Christianity with around 2.4 billion
followers, Islam with around 1.8

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:21.759 align:start position:0%
billion, Hinduism with 1.2 billion, and
Buddhism with 500 million. So, these are

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:26.560 align:start position:0%
the undisputed big four. However, within
the field of religious studies, it is

00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:31.200 align:start position:0%
often said that there are five major
world religions with the fifth one being

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:35.360 align:start position:0%
Judaism. But I want to make it clear
that the number of people who follow

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:40.640 align:start position:0%
Judaism is actually extremely small
compared to the other four just 16

00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:46.000 align:start position:0%
million. The only reason Judaism gets
included as a major world religion is

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:51.200 align:start position:0%
because of its age and because it is the
parent religion to both Christianity and

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:55.759 align:start position:0%
Islam. If we were simply going by size,
the fifth largest religion in the world

00:01:53.600 --> 00:02:01.759 align:start position:0%
and the only other one that stands out
as being really big would be Chinese

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:07.680 align:start position:0%
folk religion or as I've called it here,
Chinese synretatism. Synretism means a

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:12.239 align:start position:0%
mixture of different religious ideas.
And indeed, Chinese religion does stand

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:17.280 align:start position:0%
out in that it's not really just one
thing. I'd also like to point out that

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:22.319 align:start position:0%
over here on the right, there's another
infographic. This time a map showing the

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:27.200 align:start position:0%
dominant religion in each country.
Again, the big four, Christianity,

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:32.480 align:start position:0%
Islam, Hinduism, and Buddhism really
stand out, as does Chinese synretatism.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:38.959 align:start position:0%
All right, let's now start at the very
top where I have an image labeled

00:02:34.959 --> 00:02:45.760 align:start position:0%
prehistoric religions. This image is of
Gabbeckley Teepe in what is today

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:49.840 align:start position:0%
Turkey. Gabbec is the oldest humanmade
structure on Earth. And although we

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:54.160 align:start position:0%
don't know all the details, it almost
certainly served as some sort of

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:59.360 align:start position:0%
religious site. Now, I'm not saying that
all religions can't be traced back to

00:02:56.239 --> 00:03:04.159 align:start position:0%
whatever was happening at Gabbecepe. I'm
simply using it as an example of

00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:08.560 align:start position:0%
prehistoric religions in general. From
there, I highlight four of the earliest

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:13.920 align:start position:0%
religions to emerge during the
historical era. ancient Egyptian

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:19.120 align:start position:0%
polytheism, ancient Mesopotamian
polytheism, protoindo-uropean

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:23.840 align:start position:0%
polytheism, and Indis Valley
civilization religion. Note that I

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:28.319 align:start position:0%
didn't use the label polytheism for the
last one because currently the Indis

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:32.239 align:start position:0%
Valley script remains undeciphered and
therefore we don't actually know for

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:38.000 align:start position:0%
sure whether their religion was
polytheistic or not. I chose these four

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:43.840 align:start position:0%
because they had a direct influence on
the two oldest religions still in

00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:48.959 align:start position:0%
existence today. Judaism and Hinduism.
Both the religion of ancient Egypt and

00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:53.680 align:start position:0%
the religion of ancient Mesopotamia had
an influence on Israelite religion

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:58.959 align:start position:0%
because ancient Israel happened to be
located right in between these two

00:03:56.159 --> 00:04:04.239 align:start position:0%
centers of early civilization. And of
course it is from ancient Israelite

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:09.599 align:start position:0%
religion that Judaism developed.
Likewise both Indo-Uropean religion and

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:14.879 align:start position:0%
Indis Valley civilization religion had
an influence on Vadic religion due to

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:19.600 align:start position:0%
the fact that a subset of Indo-Uropeans
ended up migrating into India. Now

00:04:17.759 --> 00:04:24.639 align:start position:0%
what's interesting is that a different
subset of Indo-Uropeans ended up in

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:30.080 align:start position:0%
Persia where the religion of
Zoroastrianism developed and several

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:35.919 align:start position:0%
other subsets ended up in Europe where
the various forms of European paganism

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:40.240 align:start position:0%
developed such as Greek paganism which
in turn gave rise to Greek philosophy.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:45.840 align:start position:0%
Now the reason why this is interesting
is because both the Persians as well as

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:51.680 align:start position:0%
the Greeks ended up ruling the Jews and
therefore both Zoroastrianism and Greek

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:57.520 align:start position:0%
philosophy ended up influencing Judaism
which means that the world's two oldest

00:04:54.320 --> 00:05:02.919 align:start position:0%
religions Judaism and Hinduism are
connected at least remotely via

00:04:59.919 --> 00:05:02.919 align:start position:0%
protoindo-uropeans.

00:05:04.578 --> 00:05:09.600 align:start position:0%
[music]
Now, the first thing I want to do is

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:14.639 align:start position:0%
remind you that I'm using the word
denomination very loosely in these

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:19.360 align:start position:0%
videos. You see, the word denomination
really only works within a Christian

00:05:17.039 --> 00:05:23.120 align:start position:0%
context. So, you have to understand that
when I use it to talk about a

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:29.199 align:start position:0%
non-Christian religion like Judaism,
Islam or Hinduism, the analogy is not

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:34.560 align:start position:0%
perfect. So, basically, whenever I say
denomination, know that I simply mean a

00:05:31.919 --> 00:05:40.479 align:start position:0%
branch or subgroup within a larger
religion. Now when it comes to Hinduism,

00:05:37.759 --> 00:05:45.759 align:start position:0%
even the word religion itself is
problematic because it can definitely be

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:50.400 align:start position:0%
argued that Hinduism is not actually a
single religion but rather a cluster of

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:55.680 align:start position:0%
religions grouped together simply
because of their connection to India. In

00:05:53.360 --> 00:06:01.919 align:start position:0%
fact, Hindus themselves don't refer to
Hinduism as a religion. They call it a

00:05:58.639 --> 00:06:09.120 align:start position:0%
dharma which means something closer to a
cosmic order or set of divine laws. This

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:14.639 align:start position:0%
is why Hinduism is often categorized as
one of the dharmic religions together

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:19.199 align:start position:0%
with Hinduism, Buddhism, Janism and
Sikism. All of which originated on the

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:24.720 align:start position:0%
Indian subcontinent.
Now the one thing and this is often the

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:29.919 align:start position:0%
only thing that most non-Hindus know
about Hinduism is that it has a lot of

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:35.440 align:start position:0%
gods. So another thing I want to clear
up from the start is that this does not

00:06:32.639 --> 00:06:41.280 align:start position:0%
necessarily mean that all Hindus are
polytheists meaning people who worship

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:46.639 align:start position:0%
many gods. In fact a lot of Hindus are
actually monotheists meaning that they

00:06:43.919 --> 00:06:52.400 align:start position:0%
believe that all gods are aspects of one
god. Others are something closer to

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:57.919 align:start position:0%
heotheists, meaning that they have one
god that they worship as a supreme god,

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:03.039 align:start position:0%
but they also acknowledge the existence
of lesser gods. To make things even more

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:08.080 align:start position:0%
complicated, many Hindus are more
accurately pantheists, meaning that they

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:12.319 align:start position:0%
believe that God and the universe are
one and the same. And then finally,

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:17.199 align:start position:0%
there are also some Hindus who are
actually atheists, meaning that they

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:22.400 align:start position:0%
don't believe in gods at all. and
instead approach Hinduism from a

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:26.639 align:start position:0%
strictly philosophical perspective.
However, with that said, I do want to

00:07:24.639 --> 00:07:31.199 align:start position:0%
introduce you to some of the main gods
within Hinduism because this will help

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:36.479 align:start position:0%
you later when I discuss Hindu
denominations. It is often said that

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:42.800 align:start position:0%
modern Hinduism has three main gods.
These are Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:48.400 align:start position:0%
Often labeled as the creator, the
preserver and the destroyer. Although

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:53.360 align:start position:0%
not all Hindus view them this way.
Sometimes these three gods are even

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:59.440 align:start position:0%
referred to as the Hindu trinity.
Although the more appropriate word is

00:07:55.599 --> 00:08:06.000 align:start position:0%
the trrim. Brahma should not be confused
with Brahman. Brahman with the n on the

00:08:03.039 --> 00:08:12.080 align:start position:0%
end refers to the concept of an ultimate
reality which is equated with the

00:08:08.639 --> 00:08:17.759 align:start position:0%
totality of the universe. In contrast,
Brahma is a distinct god. In fact, a

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:22.160 align:start position:0%
male god who is credited with having
created the physical world and with

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:26.720 align:start position:0%
being the father of many other gods.
Strangely though, Brahma is not a god

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:31.120 align:start position:0%
who is regularly worshiped in India
today. And in fact, there are very few

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:35.599 align:start position:0%
temples that are dedicated to him
specifically. The easiest way to

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:42.240 align:start position:0%
recognize him is that he is usually
depicted as having four heads. Vishnu

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:48.160 align:start position:0%
and Shiva are much more popular. Vishnu
is usually depicted with multiple arms,

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:53.440 align:start position:0%
a blue complexion, and one hand holding
a shell. You'll also usually see him

00:08:50.399 --> 00:08:58.880 align:start position:0%
sitting on a giant multi-headed snake.
And note that I said him. Vishnu, like

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:04.240 align:start position:0%
all three of these main gods, is male.
He's also well known for having been

00:09:00.959 --> 00:09:10.320 align:start position:0%
incarnated many times on Earth. His two
most popular incarnations being Krishna

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:16.959 align:start position:0%
and Rama. Shiva can be distinguished
from Vishnu because he has a more wild

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:22.720 align:start position:0%
appearance, matted hair and clothes made
from animal skin. Also, he's almost

00:09:19.519 --> 00:09:29.920 align:start position:0%
always carrying a trident. Now, each of
the three main Hindu gods also has a

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:36.320 align:start position:0%
female consort or wife. Saruati pairs
with Brahma. Lakshmi pairs with Vishnu

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:40.399 align:start position:0%
and Parvati pairs with Shiva. If you see
a goddess sitting on a white lotus

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:46.720 align:start position:0%
flower playing a stringed instrument
near a peacock, that's Saraswati. And if

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:53.279 align:start position:0%
you see a goddess sitting on a red lotus
near elephants with coins somehow being

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:59.839 align:start position:0%
poured out, that's Lakshmi. Otherwise,
it's probably Pavari or one of Pavari's

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:06.240 align:start position:0%
many alternative forms such as Durga or
Kali. Another popular god in Hinduism is

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:11.200 align:start position:0%
Ganesh. He's easily recognizable because
he's the one with the elephant head. He

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:16.399 align:start position:0%
fits on the family tree as the son of
Shiva and Pavarati. Finally, let me

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:21.279 align:start position:0%
introduce the Hindu gods for the sun and
the moon, Surya and Chandra. Now you

00:10:19.519 --> 00:10:26.320 align:start position:0%
know why the Indian space missions to
the moon are called Chandrean. Yan

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:31.120 align:start position:0%
meaning vehicle. There are of course
many more Hindu gods beyond these ones.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:36.320 align:start position:0%
But I'm going to stop there for now.
Next I want to introduce you to the main

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:41.279 align:start position:0%
Hindu scriptures or holy writings.
Unlike Christians who have the Bible and

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:46.560 align:start position:0%
Muslims who have the Quran, there is no
single book within Hinduism that is

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:52.240 align:start position:0%
directly comparable to these two. Just
like Hinduism has many gods, it also has

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:57.920 align:start position:0%
many scriptures. These are divided into
two categories. Shr meaning that which

00:10:54.959 --> 00:11:03.760 align:start position:0%
is heard and smeari meaning that which
is remembered. Shrui is considered more

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:09.600 align:start position:0%
authoritative and it consists of the
four vdas. The rigveda which is the

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:16.640 align:start position:0%
oldest followed by the yajurveda and
sama and finally the atarveda which is

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:22.800 align:start position:0%
the most recent. In turn, each va also
has four parts or layers. The oldest

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:28.880 align:start position:0%
layers are the samahitas which are kind
of like hymns or prayers. Next, there

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:34.079 align:start position:0%
are the aryakas which are instructions
about rituals and ceremonies and then

00:11:31.279 --> 00:11:39.360 align:start position:0%
the brahmanas which are commentaries on
those instructions. Finally, there are

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:45.279 align:start position:0%
the upananishads which keep in mind were
added last. These are more philosophical

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:50.320 align:start position:0%
and represent Hinduism's transition from
a mere system of ancient rituals to what

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:56.399 align:start position:0%
we today consider to be a fullyfledged
religion. Smiri consists of an even

00:11:53.920 --> 00:12:02.399 align:start position:0%
larger collection of writings. I'm going
to mention just three. First, there are

00:11:58.959 --> 00:12:07.920 align:start position:0%
the Mahabarat and Ramayana. Two epic
poems that are sort of like the Iliad

00:12:04.959 --> 00:12:13.040 align:start position:0%
but much much longer. One small section
of the Mahabarat is known as the

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:17.360 align:start position:0%
Bhagavat Gita which is often the only
set of Hindu scriptures that most

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:23.040 align:start position:0%
westerners are familiar with. Previously
I did a whole video on the Mahabarat and

00:12:20.399 --> 00:12:27.279 align:start position:0%
the family tree of its characters. So if
you want to learn more about that, I'll

00:12:25.279 --> 00:12:33.440 align:start position:0%
leave a link to it in the description.
Finally, included in the Smiri are the

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:38.639 align:start position:0%
Puranas, a large collection of stories
and encyclopedic information that cover

00:12:36.399 --> 00:12:43.120 align:start position:0%
everything from the genealogy of the
gods to the history of royal dynasties.

00:12:41.519 --> 00:12:48.480 align:start position:0%
Okay, so now that you have some
background on the Hindu gods and Hindu

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:54.240 align:start position:0%
scriptures, let me now talk about how
the religion we call Hinduism developed.

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:58.959 align:start position:0%
Like I did in the Christian series, I'm
going to offer you two scenarios. the

00:12:56.880 --> 00:13:04.399 align:start position:0%
one that is told by those who take the
Hindu scriptures literally and the one

00:13:01.279 --> 00:13:09.519 align:start position:0%
that is told by secular academics.
According to the traditional Hindu view,

00:13:06.959 --> 00:13:14.079 align:start position:0%
the people living in India today are the
direct descendants of the people who

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:19.279 align:start position:0%
were living there 10,000 years ago. And
throughout that entire time, the Hindu

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:24.720 align:start position:0%
religion has pretty much been the same.
In fact, one view within Hinduism is

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:30.399 align:start position:0%
that history is cyclical and made up of
four ages with each one being worse than

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:35.680 align:start position:0%
the one before. Once the four ages are
completed, the whole process repeats

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:42.800 align:start position:0%
itself. Currently, we are in the fourth
age, which started around 3100 B.CE

00:13:40.079 --> 00:13:47.760 align:start position:0%
around the time of the Mahabarat war.
According to the traditional Hindu view,

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:52.480 align:start position:0%
the most important scriptures, the vadas
are authorless and were revealed to

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:58.800 align:start position:0%
certain sages before this through
intense meditation. However, near the

00:13:55.200 --> 00:14:03.279 align:start position:0%
end of the third age, a sage named Viasa
compiled them in the form that we have

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:08.880 align:start position:0%
them in today in addition to writing the
Mahabarat and the Puranas. Now, as you

00:14:06.639 --> 00:14:13.360 align:start position:0%
might have guessed, the secular view of
how Hinduism developed is quite

00:14:11.199 --> 00:14:19.519 align:start position:0%
different. According to the academic
consensus, what we call Hinduism today

00:14:16.639 --> 00:14:24.639 align:start position:0%
evolved slowly over time and has its
roots in at least three different

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:29.920 align:start position:0%
places. One of these is the Indis Valley
civilization which is one of the three

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:35.360 align:start position:0%
oldest civilizations on earth. The other
two being Egypt and Sumer. However,

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:40.560 align:start position:0%
unlike with ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs
and Sumerian kuneaform, we cannot read

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:45.360 align:start position:0%
the writing left behind by the indis
valley civilization and hence we cannot

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:49.760 align:start position:0%
know for sure what their religion was
and how it might be connected to

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:55.279 align:start position:0%
Hinduism. There are some tantalizing
hints though such as this Indis Valley

00:14:52.639 --> 00:15:00.000 align:start position:0%
seal which shows a figure who shares
certain attributes in common with the

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:04.880 align:start position:0%
Hindu god Shiva. Then there are local
folk religions that likely developed

00:15:02.399 --> 00:15:09.920 align:start position:0%
throughout the Indian subcontinent, each
with their own local god. To this day,

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:15.279 align:start position:0%
there are rural villages in India that
still follow a kind of folk Hinduism

00:15:12.639 --> 00:15:20.399 align:start position:0%
that combines certain Hindu practices
with the worship of a local god who

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:24.800 align:start position:0%
actually predates Hinduism. Finally,
there's protoindo-uropean

00:15:22.639 --> 00:15:29.680 align:start position:0%
religion. The same religion that gave
birth to the pantheon of gods worshiped

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:34.880 align:start position:0%
by the Greeks, Romans, and Germanic
tribes. For example, the main gods

00:15:32.079 --> 00:15:41.440 align:start position:0%
worshiped by the protoindo-uropeans
include a skyfather named Dus, a young

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:49.279 align:start position:0%
goddess of the dawn named House, and a
set of twins associated with horses. In

00:15:45.199 --> 00:15:54.800 align:start position:0%
Greece, Duseus became known as Zeus. And
in many European languages today, the

00:15:51.759 --> 00:16:01.279 align:start position:0%
word for god is still something like dia
or dios. There's also a Greek goddess of

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:07.360 align:start position:0%
the dawn named Aos and a pair of twins
in Anglo-Saxon legend named Hangust and

00:16:04.399 --> 00:16:12.160 align:start position:0%
Horsa. What about in India though? Well,
what do you know? In the Rigveda, which

00:16:09.839 --> 00:16:19.440 align:start position:0%
remember is the oldest set of scriptures
in Hinduism, it too mentions a skyfather

00:16:15.839 --> 00:16:25.759 align:start position:0%
deity named Daos. And it also has a
goddess of the dawn called Ushas and a

00:16:22.399 --> 00:16:30.959 align:start position:0%
set of twins called the Ashvins. Ashvin
being the Sanskrit word for horsemen.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:36.399 align:start position:0%
But don't get me wrong, I am not saying
that I agree with the now debunked Aryan

00:16:33.839 --> 00:16:41.759 align:start position:0%
invasion theory. That theory, which
clearly had racist overtones, claimed

00:16:39.199 --> 00:16:46.639 align:start position:0%
that lighter-kinned Indo-Uropeans called
Aryans conquered the earlier

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:51.040 align:start position:0%
darkerkinned inhabitants of India in
some sort of dramatic fashion, causing

00:16:48.639 --> 00:16:56.560 align:start position:0%
the sudden demise of the Indis Valley
civilization. Instead, the academic

00:16:53.759 --> 00:17:04.480 align:start position:0%
consensus today is that there was a very
slow migration of Indo-Uropeans into

00:17:00.079 --> 00:17:09.839 align:start position:0%
India between the years 2,00
B.CE. CE and that these people likely

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:15.439 align:start position:0%
intermixed with the local populations
resulting in the creation of the Vadic

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:21.199 align:start position:0%
civilization. This new hypothesis is
backed up by both linguistic evidence

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:26.400 align:start position:0%
and DNA evidence. Now, as you probably
guessed, the Vadic civilization is so

00:17:24.079 --> 00:17:31.760 align:start position:0%
named because it produced the Hindu
scriptures called the Vadas. But keep in

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:37.200 align:start position:0%
mind that the Vdic religion was not the
same thing as modern Hinduism. For

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:43.120 align:start position:0%
example, the main gods talked about in
the Vadas are not Vishnu and Shiva.

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:48.799 align:start position:0%
Rather, they are Indra, Veruna, and
Agni. So, although it's often said that

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:56.240 align:start position:0%
Hinduism is the world's oldest religion,
dating back 4,000 plus years, this is

00:17:51.760 --> 00:18:02.000 align:start position:0%
not exactly true. The roots of Hinduism
and some of its customs do go back that

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:07.679 align:start position:0%
far. But Hinduism as we know it today
does not. The same is true for Judaism.

00:18:05.039 --> 00:18:13.520 align:start position:0%
Judaism has its roots in ancient
Israelite religion which originated

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:18.160 align:start position:0%
around 3,000 years ago. However, Judaism
as we know it today is not identical to

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:25.200 align:start position:0%
the religion practiced by the ancient
Israelites. It developed mostly between

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:30.480 align:start position:0%
the years 600 B.CE CE and 200 CE. So my
point is dating religions is not as

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:36.799 align:start position:0%
simple as you might think because
religions change over time and this is

00:18:33.679 --> 00:18:41.280 align:start position:0%
certainly true of Hinduism. The Vadic
religion eventually evolved into

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:46.960 align:start position:0%
Brahminism by which point the priestly
cast known as the Brahinss was firmly

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:52.000 align:start position:0%
established. But Brahmanism was by no
means the only religion in India at this

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:58.000 align:start position:0%
point. It was mainly practiced in the
kingdom of Kuru. Further east, the

00:18:54.559 --> 00:19:03.360 align:start position:0%
shamana movement was taking hold. Shana
meaning seeker. Shmanas rejected the

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:08.320 align:start position:0%
authority of the vadas as well as the
brahinss and instead promoted rigid

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:13.200 align:start position:0%
self-discipline and the rejection of
worldly pleasures. It was out of the

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:18.559 align:start position:0%
shana movement that the religions of
Buddhism and Janism developed. However,

00:19:16.559 --> 00:19:23.840 align:start position:0%
it also had a big impact on the
development of Hinduism leading to

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:30.160 align:start position:0%
what's been called the Hindu synthesis
which occurred over the period from

00:19:25.679 --> 00:19:34.960 align:start position:0%
around 500 B.CE and 500 CE which is when
many religious ideas and customs came

00:19:32.559 --> 00:19:40.640 align:start position:0%
together to form what we know as
Hinduism today. It was during this

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:45.679 align:start position:0%
period that the Mahabarat, Ramayan and
Puranas were written and it was after

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:51.120 align:start position:0%
this period that Indian religious views
could now be divided into clear

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:56.640 align:start position:0%
categories called Astika and Nastika.
Astika schools of thought are considered

00:19:53.520 --> 00:20:03.360 align:start position:0%
orthodox by Hindus because they all
accept the authority of the vadas. The

00:19:59.679 --> 00:20:12.160 align:start position:0%
six Astika or schools of Hinduism are
Nyana, Vashika, Samia, Yoga, Mimsa and

00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:17.840 align:start position:0%
Vanta. However, keep in mind that these
are not denominations. They are more

00:20:15.039 --> 00:20:22.559 align:start position:0%
like philosophies that people within
different Hindu denominations can

00:20:19.919 --> 00:20:28.240 align:start position:0%
follow. In contrast to the Astika
schools, the Nastika schools reject the

00:20:25.919 --> 00:20:35.039 align:start position:0%
vadas and are therefore considered
heterodox by Hindus. These include the

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:39.679 align:start position:0%
religions of Buddhism and Janism, but
also several lesserknown schools of

00:20:37.039 --> 00:20:45.200 align:start position:0%
thought. Now, if you're a westerner, out
of the six astika, there's probably one

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:50.480 align:start position:0%
that you recognize, yoga. Well, the
first thing you need to know about yoga

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:56.640 align:start position:0%
is that it is not simply a series of
exercises, which is what most Westerners

00:20:53.520 --> 00:21:00.960 align:start position:0%
think yoga is. Yoga is actually a
complete system of philosophy. And in

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:06.159 align:start position:0%
fact, it's one of the more popular
systems of Hindu philosophy. As you

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:11.760 align:start position:0%
probably know, most Hindus believe in
reincarnation and that we are stuck in a

00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:17.840 align:start position:0%
seemingly endless cycle of birth, death,
and rebirth. The goal of Hinduism is

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:22.880 align:start position:0%
therefore to achieve mosha which is the
release from the cycle. Well, yoga

00:21:21.039 --> 00:21:28.720 align:start position:0%
posits that there are actually four
different religious paths that a person

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:34.240 align:start position:0%
can follow to achieve moka. The first is
karma yoga which basically involves

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:40.000 align:start position:0%
working hard, doing good and serving
others. Then there's bakti yoga which

00:21:37.679 --> 00:21:45.600 align:start position:0%
involves showing love and devotion
towards a particular god. Finally

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:50.720 align:start position:0%
there's ghana yoga which involves
pursuing knowledge and raja yoga which

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:55.760 align:start position:0%
involves meditation. But again these
four paths do not represent four

00:21:53.120 --> 00:22:02.000 align:start position:0%
different denominations. Hindus from
various denominations may follow one or

00:21:58.559 --> 00:22:08.240 align:start position:0%
more of these paths. If there's anything
akin to denominations within Hinduism,

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:13.280 align:start position:0%
we could place them under bakti yoga
because the most common way that Hindus

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:18.799 align:start position:0%
can be divided into various subgroups is
by which god or gods they are

00:22:15.679 --> 00:22:25.760 align:start position:0%
particularly devoted to. This is why it
is often said that Hinduism has four

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:31.760 align:start position:0%
main denominations. Vishnavism, shyism,
shockism and smartism. Let's look at

00:22:29.039 --> 00:22:38.480 align:start position:0%
Vishnavism first because it's the
largest denomination representing around

00:22:34.240 --> 00:22:43.679 align:start position:0%
70% of all Hindus. Vishnavists worship
the god Vishnu as the supreme deity.

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:49.360 align:start position:0%
This includes his various incarnated
forms called avatars which is when he

00:22:46.559 --> 00:22:54.559 align:start position:0%
was born on earth as a human or animal.
His two most popular avatars are Rama

00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:59.760 align:start position:0%
and Krishna. Now, as I mentioned
earlier, Vishnu was not actually one of

00:22:57.120 --> 00:23:04.240 align:start position:0%
the main Vadic gods, although he is
mentioned a few times in the Rigveda.

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:09.919 align:start position:0%
However, over time, he took on the
attributes and legends of other gods and

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:15.440 align:start position:0%
became more and more important. For
example, one group of ancient Indians

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:20.799 align:start position:0%
worshiped a god named Vasu Deva. This
god was eventually merged with another

00:23:17.679 --> 00:23:25.840 align:start position:0%
god named Krishna, who was worshiped by
a different group of people. But then

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:30.799 align:start position:0%
still later, Vasu Deva Krishna merged
with Vishnu and was understood to be

00:23:28.320 --> 00:23:34.080 align:start position:0%
just one of Vishnu's 10 main
incarnations.

00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:39.280 align:start position:0%
Now, lest you think that this is
strange, let me point out that two or

00:23:36.320 --> 00:23:42.880 align:start position:0%
more gods merging into one is actually a
pretty common thing throughout the

00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:48.080 align:start position:0%
history of religion. For instance, in
Canaan, there was originally a god named

00:23:45.679 --> 00:23:54.400 align:start position:0%
L, who was separate from the god
represented by the letters YHWH.

00:23:51.600 --> 00:24:01.200 align:start position:0%
But then eventually over time these two
gods merged and were seen as being one

00:23:58.000 --> 00:24:07.760 align:start position:0%
and the same. Which explains why to this
day the Bible sometimes calls God L or

00:24:04.720 --> 00:24:12.880 align:start position:0%
Elohim and then other times calls him
YHWH.

00:24:09.919 --> 00:24:19.440 align:start position:0%
The second largest Hindu denomination is
shyism found mostly in South India and

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:26.240 align:start position:0%
followed by around 25% of all Hindus.
Shivists worship the god Shiva as the

00:24:22.880 --> 00:24:32.159 align:start position:0%
supreme deity. Unlike Vishnu, Shiva is
not mentioned in the Rigveda at all.

00:24:29.120 --> 00:24:37.440 align:start position:0%
However, the Rigveda does mention a god
named Rudra who is very similar to Shiva

00:24:35.120 --> 00:24:43.440 align:start position:0%
and is thus strongly associated with
him. Another thing that makes shyism

00:24:40.320 --> 00:24:49.200 align:start position:0%
different from vishnavism is that shiva
is often woripped in a nonhuman form

00:24:46.559 --> 00:24:54.000 align:start position:0%
being displayed in many temples as a
simple stone called a lingum. Many

00:24:51.840 --> 00:24:59.440 align:start position:0%
people assume that the lingum is
supposed to represent a male fallus but

00:24:56.880 --> 00:25:06.000 align:start position:0%
this is actually not true. It's simply
meant to communicate the idea that Shiva

00:25:02.240 --> 00:25:12.559 align:start position:0%
has no real form. The remaining 5% of
Hindus follow either shockism or

00:25:08.880 --> 00:25:18.320 align:start position:0%
smartism. Shockism is closely related to
shyism. But whereas shyists worship the

00:25:16.159 --> 00:25:24.080 align:start position:0%
supreme deity in the form of the male
god Shiva, shaktists worship the supreme

00:25:21.440 --> 00:25:29.440 align:start position:0%
deity in the form of the female goddess
Shakti, which is another name for

00:25:26.480 --> 00:25:34.640 align:start position:0%
Parvati, Shiva's wife. Like I mentioned
earlier, this supreme goddess takes many

00:25:32.240 --> 00:25:39.760 align:start position:0%
forms. Sometimes she's the sweet and
loving Paratti, but other times she's

00:25:36.960 --> 00:25:45.279 align:start position:0%
the warrior goddess Durga or even the
scaryl looking Kali. Finally, there's

00:25:42.320 --> 00:25:51.520 align:start position:0%
the Hindu denomination known as Smartism
in which five gods are worshiped

00:25:47.440 --> 00:25:57.679 align:start position:0%
equally. Ganesh, Shiva, Shakti, Vishnu
and Surya. Note that the word smartism

00:25:54.480 --> 00:26:02.559 align:start position:0%
is based on the word smiri which we came
across earlier and which refers to the

00:26:00.080 --> 00:26:08.720 align:start position:0%
body of Hindu scriptures that came after
the vadas. Now as a whole Hinduism is

00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:14.720 align:start position:0%
the world's third largest religion with
around 1.1 billion followers. However,

00:26:12.640 --> 00:26:20.400 align:start position:0%
unlike the other two big religions,
Christianity and Islam, Hinduism is

00:26:17.520 --> 00:26:25.760 align:start position:0%
mostly limited to just one area of the
world, South Asia. And whenever you do

00:26:23.520 --> 00:26:30.559 align:start position:0%
find Hinduism being practiced outside of
South Asia, it's almost always among

00:26:28.159 --> 00:26:35.919 align:start position:0%
people of South Asian descent. The one
exception to this is the many neo-Hindu

00:26:33.679 --> 00:26:40.559 align:start position:0%
movements that have sprung up in Western
countries since the middle of the 20th

00:26:38.159 --> 00:26:46.880 align:start position:0%
century. Most of these are founded by
individual gurus or teachers many of

00:26:43.440 --> 00:26:50.320 align:start position:0%
whom were or are quite controversial. It
would take a whole other video to go

00:26:48.480 --> 00:26:56.320 align:start position:0%
through all of them. So let me just
point out two. The first is Bakti

00:26:52.960 --> 00:27:00.880 align:start position:0%
Vadanta Swami Praupada. He founded the
international society for Krishna

00:26:58.400 --> 00:27:05.760 align:start position:0%
consciousness better known as the Hari
Krishnas because they are known for

00:27:03.039 --> 00:27:11.440 align:start position:0%
chanting that phrase over and over as
well as Harama. The word Har is another

00:27:09.440 --> 00:27:17.039 align:start position:0%
name for Vishnu. And as we learned
earlier, both Krishna and Rama are

00:27:13.840 --> 00:27:22.880 align:start position:0%
avatars of Vishnu. So it won't surprise
you when I tell you that Hari Krishna's

00:27:19.520 --> 00:27:28.720 align:start position:0%
follow a type of vishnavism. However,
their type of vishnavism traces its

00:27:25.760 --> 00:27:34.640 align:start position:0%
roots back to Gaudia vishnavism which
started around the year 1500 and which

00:27:31.360 --> 00:27:39.679 align:start position:0%
focuses on Krishna as the supreme deity.
Swami Prabhupada was himself a

00:27:37.360 --> 00:27:45.279 align:start position:0%
controversial figure known for making
racist, anti-Semitic, sexist and

00:27:42.080 --> 00:27:49.600 align:start position:0%
classist comments and the controversies
continued after his death with Iscon

00:27:47.760 --> 00:27:53.840 align:start position:0%
leaders eventually admitting that
physical and sexual abuse was taking

00:27:51.520 --> 00:27:58.720 align:start position:0%
place within their organization. They
have since taken steps to rebuild their

00:27:56.080 --> 00:28:03.919 align:start position:0%
reputation and hopefully better protect
children. The other guru I want to

00:28:01.200 --> 00:28:09.200 align:start position:0%
mention is Maharishi Mahesh Yogi who
many people know of simply because of

00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:14.080 align:start position:0%
his association with the Beatles. More
importantly though, he's the founder of

00:28:11.360 --> 00:28:19.360 align:start position:0%
transcendental meditation movement.
Although marketed as a non-religious

00:28:16.480 --> 00:28:25.240 align:start position:0%
method, it has its roots in meditation
techniques that have been practiced

00:28:20.960 --> 00:28:25.240 align:start position:0%
within Hinduism for centuries.

00:28:25.639 --> 00:28:32.480 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; So let's start with the Vic religion

00:28:29.600 --> 00:28:38.960 align:start position:0%
which I introduced in my Hinduism video.
It developed in India around 1500 B.CE

00:28:36.080 --> 00:28:43.120 align:start position:0%
after a group of Indo-Uropeans slowly
migrated into the area probably

00:28:41.360 --> 00:28:46.960 align:start position:0%
intermingling with the descendants of
the once mighty Indis Valley

00:28:44.799 --> 00:28:51.360 align:start position:0%
civilization as well as with other
native Indians living along the Ganges

00:28:49.279 --> 00:28:55.840 align:start position:0%
River. The Vadic religion likely
borrowed elements from all three of

00:28:53.360 --> 00:29:00.960 align:start position:0%
these groups which is an important point
to remember. We call this early form of

00:28:58.480 --> 00:29:05.760 align:start position:0%
Hinduism Vadic because it was during
this period that the oldest and most

00:29:03.120 --> 00:29:11.520 align:start position:0%
sacred Hindu scriptures called the Vedas
were composed. However, by around 500

00:29:09.039 --> 00:29:16.880 align:start position:0%
B.CE CE the Vadic religion had evolved
into Brahmanism in which a certain class

00:29:13.919 --> 00:29:22.080 align:start position:0%
of people known as brahinss controlled
the priesthood as well as many other

00:29:19.120 --> 00:29:27.360 align:start position:0%
aspects of society. Below them were the
cashatria consisting of secular rulers

00:29:24.720 --> 00:29:34.000 align:start position:0%
and warriors the visha the farmers and
merchants and finally the sudra laborers

00:29:30.559 --> 00:29:39.440 align:start position:0%
and servants. However, not everyone was
happy with the authority of the brahinss

00:29:36.799 --> 00:29:44.880 align:start position:0%
and with the teachings of the vadas.
This gave rise to the shrammana movement

00:29:42.159 --> 00:29:49.440 align:start position:0%
which was particularly popular along the
eastern genetic plane. In order to

00:29:47.679 --> 00:29:55.600 align:start position:0%
explain, let's take a look at a map of
India around 500 B.CE. By this point,

00:29:52.559 --> 00:30:01.279 align:start position:0%
most of the north was divided into 16
independent states which were known as

00:29:58.240 --> 00:30:06.480 align:start position:0%
Mahajanapadas, meaning great realms.
Brahmanism was strongest in the kingdom

00:30:03.919 --> 00:30:11.919 align:start position:0%
of Kuru which had previously been much
larger and was the setting for the great

00:30:08.960 --> 00:30:17.840 align:start position:0%
Hindu epic the Mahabarat. But to the
east there were other states like

00:30:14.480 --> 00:30:23.679 align:start position:0%
Kosala, Vji and Magada where support for
the brahinss was weaker. It was here

00:30:20.640 --> 00:30:28.559 align:start position:0%
that the shamana movement took hold.
Basically, a shamana was a person who

00:30:26.320 --> 00:30:34.159 align:start position:0%
dropped out of everyday society in order
to instead live a very simple life

00:30:31.360 --> 00:30:38.559 align:start position:0%
focused on spiritual development. This
resulted in the development of several

00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:43.360 align:start position:0%
new schools of philosophy. But it also
ended up influencing Brahminism as well

00:30:41.039 --> 00:30:49.200 align:start position:0%
leading to what's been called the Hindu
synthesis which is when what we know

00:30:45.760 --> 00:30:54.320 align:start position:0%
today as Hinduism really took shape. So
from this point forward from the Hindu

00:30:51.520 --> 00:30:59.760 align:start position:0%
perspective Indian schools of philosophy
were now divided into two categories

00:30:56.640 --> 00:31:03.760 align:start position:0%
ostika and gnostika. Ostika schools
accept the authority of the vadas and

00:31:02.320 --> 00:31:08.799 align:start position:0%
are hence considered to be a part of
Hinduism. Whereas the nastika schools

00:31:06.480 --> 00:31:13.279 align:start position:0%
reject the vadas and are thus considered
to be separate religions. The two

00:31:11.200 --> 00:31:18.480 align:start position:0%
gnostika schools that most people are
familiar with today are Janism and

00:31:16.159 --> 00:31:22.320 align:start position:0%
Buddhism. But in earlier times there
were other schools of thought that were

00:31:20.080 --> 00:31:28.000 align:start position:0%
just as popular. These include the
atheist Charvaka school, the agnostic

00:31:25.200 --> 00:31:32.720 align:start position:0%
Ajinana school, and the fatalistic
Ajivika school. Okay, with that

00:31:30.320 --> 00:31:38.960 align:start position:0%
background, let's now focus exclusively
on Buddhism. Unlike Hinduism, which has

00:31:36.159 --> 00:31:43.440 align:start position:0%
no founder, Buddhism does. It was
founded by the person who most people

00:31:40.960 --> 00:31:48.720 align:start position:0%
simply know as the Buddha. But this was
not his actual name. At birth he was

00:31:46.080 --> 00:31:53.919 align:start position:0%
called Sedartha Gotaimma and he was a
prince living within the kingdom of

00:31:50.559 --> 00:31:59.440 align:start position:0%
Kosala. More specifically he belonged to
a region and ethnic group within Kosala

00:31:56.960 --> 00:32:03.840 align:start position:0%
known as the Shakyas whose territory
actually fell within what we today call

00:32:01.360 --> 00:32:10.080 align:start position:0%
Nepal. This is why in the earliest
records the Buddha is called Shakyamuni

00:32:06.720 --> 00:32:14.799 align:start position:0%
meaning the sage of the Shakias. I won't
go through his full story but here are

00:32:12.480 --> 00:32:20.080 align:start position:0%
the highlights. At the age of 29,
Sedartha left his family and life of

00:32:16.960 --> 00:32:24.799 align:start position:0%
luxury to become a shamana. At first, he
practiced aeticism, denying himself all

00:32:22.880 --> 00:32:30.320 align:start position:0%
but the smallest amount of food needed
to survive. But then at the age of 35,

00:32:28.080 --> 00:32:35.039 align:start position:0%
while sitting under a tree, he is said
to have achieved enlightenment. It's at

00:32:32.880 --> 00:32:39.840 align:start position:0%
this point that he became the Buddha,
which is a title meaning the enlightened

00:32:37.360 --> 00:32:44.880 align:start position:0%
one. After this, he preached about the
middle way, which promotes living in

00:32:42.080 --> 00:32:49.679 align:start position:0%
between the extremes of overindulgence
on one side and self-denial on the other

00:32:47.279 --> 00:32:54.080 align:start position:0%
side. He also laid the foundations for
Buddhist thought called dharma, which

00:32:52.080 --> 00:32:59.120 align:start position:0%
can be summed up by the four noble
truths and the eight-fold path. During

00:32:56.960 --> 00:33:04.799 align:start position:0%
the Buddha's lifetime, he not only
taught the dharma, he also built up a

00:33:01.840 --> 00:33:10.080 align:start position:0%
community of followers known as the SA.
You may have heard Buddhists refer to

00:33:06.720 --> 00:33:14.880 align:start position:0%
the triple gem or three jewels. This is
a reference to the Buddha, the Dharma,

00:33:12.480 --> 00:33:21.519 align:start position:0%
and the Sana. According to tradition,
the Buddha died at age 80 around the

00:33:17.760 --> 00:33:27.120 align:start position:0%
year 480 B.CE. At this point, the first
Buddhist council was held with 500 of

00:33:24.480 --> 00:33:30.880 align:start position:0%
his followers attending. The purpose was
to make sure that all of the teachings

00:33:29.039 --> 00:33:37.120 align:start position:0%
of the Buddha and the rules for the
community were remembered. One of his 10

00:33:33.679 --> 00:33:41.600 align:start position:0%
core disciples named Ananda recited all
of the teachings which are known as

00:33:39.200 --> 00:33:47.200 align:start position:0%
sutras and another disciple named
Upupali recited the community rules

00:33:44.159 --> 00:33:52.880 align:start position:0%
which are known as vignia. According to
tradition, a second Buddhist council was

00:33:49.679 --> 00:33:57.679 align:start position:0%
held approximately 100 years after the
Buddha's death. This time there were

00:33:54.960 --> 00:34:02.240 align:start position:0%
disagreements over the community rules
and this led to the first Buddhist

00:33:59.840 --> 00:34:07.760 align:start position:0%
schism. The majority group became known
as the Maha Sangaka meaning the great SA

00:34:05.840 --> 00:34:14.240 align:start position:0%
and the minority group became known as
the Stata Viraada meaning school of the

00:34:11.359 --> 00:34:18.879 align:start position:0%
elders because it consisted mostly of
the more senior monks. Take note that

00:34:16.720 --> 00:34:23.520 align:start position:0%
all of the modern branches of Buddhism
descend from the Staviravada. Although

00:34:21.440 --> 00:34:29.200 align:start position:0%
there is some debate over whether or not
the Mahasangaka had an influence on the

00:34:26.240 --> 00:34:34.240 align:start position:0%
development of Mahayana, a term that I
will explain in a bit. But back to early

00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:38.480 align:start position:0%
Buddhism, eventually more and more
divisions occurred to the point where in

00:34:36.399 --> 00:34:43.919 align:start position:0%
ancient times it is thought that there
were at least 18 separate schools.

00:34:41.679 --> 00:34:48.480 align:start position:0%
Around the time of Ashoka, the great
Indian emperor who united most of India

00:34:46.480 --> 00:34:55.679 align:start position:0%
for the very first time. The three main
ones were the Vibajia, Servastiv and

00:34:52.320 --> 00:35:00.480 align:start position:0%
Pudgalavvada. Ashoka is an extremely
important figure in the history of early

00:34:57.920 --> 00:35:05.040 align:start position:0%
Buddhism because he himself converted to
the new religion and promoted missionary

00:35:02.880 --> 00:35:09.680 align:start position:0%
efforts to spread Buddhism to other
lands. The most important of these

00:35:07.359 --> 00:35:15.119 align:start position:0%
missions was led by his firstborn son
Mahinda who became a monk and brought

00:35:12.320 --> 00:35:19.440 align:start position:0%
Buddhism to Sri Lanka. Now I should
point out that one does not need to

00:35:17.040 --> 00:35:24.480 align:start position:0%
become a monk to follow Buddhism
although some still do as it is

00:35:21.839 --> 00:35:29.280 align:start position:0%
generally seen as being a faster way to
reach enlightenment.

00:35:26.400 --> 00:35:34.800 align:start position:0%
In Sri Lanka, the school founded by
Mahinda became known as the Tamra

00:35:32.160 --> 00:35:41.200 align:start position:0%
Shhatyia school and it was a branch of
the Vibbajia school. It was in Sri Lanka

00:35:38.320 --> 00:35:46.880 align:start position:0%
that the Polycanon was produced which
today is the oldest surviving complete

00:35:44.240 --> 00:35:52.720 align:start position:0%
set of Buddhist scriptures. Take note
that Pali is a language closely related

00:35:49.760 --> 00:35:57.599 align:start position:0%
to but not quite the same as Sanskrit.
Let's now take a moment to look at the

00:35:54.480 --> 00:36:03.440 align:start position:0%
contents of the polycanon. A full set of
Buddhist scriptures is called a

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:08.079 align:start position:0%
tripetaka which means three baskets.
That's because it's comprised of three

00:36:05.440 --> 00:36:13.200 align:start position:0%
main parts. The vineya pitaka which
contains the community rules, the sutra

00:36:10.720 --> 00:36:19.440 align:start position:0%
pitaka which contains the Buddha's
teachings and the abidama which contains

00:36:15.920 --> 00:36:25.520 align:start position:0%
analysis of those teachings. The vineia
paka contains rules for both male monks

00:36:22.800 --> 00:36:30.240 align:start position:0%
who are called bikus as well as for
female monks or nuns who are called

00:36:27.520 --> 00:36:35.839 align:start position:0%
picunis. It also contains a few sections
covering early Buddhist history. In the

00:36:32.880 --> 00:36:41.839 align:start position:0%
polycanan the sutra pitaka is divided
into five parts called nikayas meaning

00:36:39.119 --> 00:36:46.480 align:start position:0%
volumes. These can then be broken down
further into smaller books. Of these

00:36:44.640 --> 00:36:52.400 align:start position:0%
smaller bugs, the one that I'd like to
highlight is the Dharma, which is

00:36:49.599 --> 00:36:56.400 align:start position:0%
located in the fifth nikaya. It's the
most well-known of all the Buddhist

00:36:54.480 --> 00:37:00.480 align:start position:0%
scriptures, and it's a good starting
point for those who want to dip their

00:36:58.320 --> 00:37:06.560 align:start position:0%
feet in the water. Finally, I'd like to
point out that the polycanon version of

00:37:02.800 --> 00:37:11.440 align:start position:0%
the Abidama has seven parts. Okay, let's
now go back to the family tree chart.

00:37:08.880 --> 00:37:17.280 align:start position:0%
From Sri Lanka, Buddhism eventually
spread to Burma, Thailand, Laos, and

00:37:14.560 --> 00:37:22.480 align:start position:0%
Cambodia. The type of Buddhism found in
all of these countries is therefore very

00:37:19.520 --> 00:37:27.520 align:start position:0%
similar. Nowadays, it is called Thera
Buddhism. Take note that the word Thera

00:37:25.280 --> 00:37:32.480 align:start position:0%
is actually just the polyversion of the
Sanskrit word staviravada, which as you

00:37:30.400 --> 00:37:38.079 align:start position:0%
might remember means school of the
elders. Thera Buddhism therefore sees

00:37:35.359 --> 00:37:43.119 align:start position:0%
itself as the original Buddhism.
Generally speaking, it is more strict

00:37:40.320 --> 00:37:48.320 align:start position:0%
and more earthly focused than the other
forms of Buddhism. Although you can see

00:37:45.920 --> 00:37:52.800 align:start position:0%
here that there are three main types of
Buddhism in the world today, considering

00:37:50.320 --> 00:37:57.520 align:start position:0%
that Tibetan Buddhism is relatively
speaking quite small, it is often said

00:37:55.040 --> 00:38:03.520 align:start position:0%
that there are really just two main
types of Buddhism, Thera and Mahayana.

00:38:01.119 --> 00:38:09.680 align:start position:0%
I'm therefore going to focus on Mahayana
next. The exact origins of Mahayana are

00:38:07.119 --> 00:38:14.560 align:start position:0%
unclear. It wasn't really a separate
school, but rather a movement that took

00:38:12.240 --> 00:38:19.359 align:start position:0%
place within many schools. One theory is
that it developed out of the now extinct

00:38:16.880 --> 00:38:24.240 align:start position:0%
Mahasangaka school. But another is that
it might have originated among lay

00:38:21.440 --> 00:38:29.040 align:start position:0%
people, meaning non-mongs. Whatever the
origin, the common factor among Mahayana

00:38:27.040 --> 00:38:34.240 align:start position:0%
Buddhists is that they have an
additional set of scriptures known as

00:38:31.280 --> 00:38:39.200 align:start position:0%
the Mahayana Sutras. According to
Mahayana Buddhism, these special sutras

00:38:37.200 --> 00:38:44.400 align:start position:0%
were initially hidden away after the
Buddhist death only to be revealed later

00:38:41.839 --> 00:38:50.079 align:start position:0%
when the time was right. One of the
early schools to accept the Mahayana

00:38:46.960 --> 00:38:54.079 align:start position:0%
Sutras was the Dharma Guptaka school
which was originally centered in Gandara

00:38:52.240 --> 00:38:59.119 align:start position:0%
in what is today Pakistan and
Afghanistan. This is why there were

00:38:56.320 --> 00:39:03.680 align:start position:0%
until very recently some very old Buddha
statues in this region. Unfortunately,

00:39:01.680 --> 00:39:09.280 align:start position:0%
these were destroyed by the Taliban in
2001. There is some debate over whether

00:39:06.640 --> 00:39:14.880 align:start position:0%
the Dharma Guptaka school came out of
the Vibajia school or whether it came

00:39:12.240 --> 00:39:20.000 align:start position:0%
out of the Sarvastiva school. I've
therefore showed it coming from both.

00:39:17.200 --> 00:39:26.160 align:start position:0%
From the Gandara region, the Dharma
Guptaka school eventually spread to

00:39:22.160 --> 00:39:31.040 align:start position:0%
China, Korea, Japan, and Vietnam. There
were other schools that spread to these

00:39:28.000 --> 00:39:36.320 align:start position:0%
areas as well, but they all went extinct
and therefore today all East Asian

00:39:33.200 --> 00:39:41.520 align:start position:0%
Mahayana monks follow the Dharma Guptaka
community rules. Strangely, although

00:39:38.880 --> 00:39:46.400 align:start position:0%
Buddhism originated in India and was
once a dominant force there, today the

00:39:43.920 --> 00:39:51.280 align:start position:0%
vast majority of Buddhists now live
outside of India. In fact, it is now

00:39:49.280 --> 00:39:56.240 align:start position:0%
China that has the most amount of
Buddhists in the world. I therefore want

00:39:53.760 --> 00:40:01.040 align:start position:0%
to talk a bit about the Chinese cannon
which is the main alternative to the

00:39:58.160 --> 00:40:06.320 align:start position:0%
polycanon. Like the polycanon, it too
contains a tripotaka. However, take note

00:40:04.400 --> 00:40:12.720 align:start position:0%
that the sections covering the teachings
of the Buddha are called agamas instead

00:40:09.119 --> 00:40:17.680 align:start position:0%
of nikayas. The Chinese cannon has only
four agamas which roughly correspond to

00:40:15.599 --> 00:40:23.359 align:start position:0%
the first four nikayas from the
polycanon. The vineya and abu dharma

00:40:20.720 --> 00:40:28.240 align:start position:0%
sections however are totally different.
Whereas the polycanon includes the

00:40:25.440 --> 00:40:33.359 align:start position:0%
theravada community rules. The Chinese
cannon includes the dharma guptaka rules

00:40:31.200 --> 00:40:38.240 align:start position:0%
as well as rules from several now
extinct schools. However, the main

00:40:36.079 --> 00:40:42.480 align:start position:0%
difference between the polycanon and the
Chinese cannon is that the Chinese

00:40:40.160 --> 00:40:47.920 align:start position:0%
cannon includes several additional
sections, most notably the Mahayana

00:40:45.200 --> 00:40:51.760 align:start position:0%
sutras which I mentioned earlier. There
are many of these, but the most

00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:56.880 align:start position:0%
important are the Lotus Sutra, the
Perfection of Wisdom Sutra, the Flower

00:40:54.079 --> 00:41:01.200 align:start position:0%
Garland Sutra, and the Nirvana Sutra.
But that's not all. The Chinese cannon

00:40:59.200 --> 00:41:06.400 align:start position:0%
also includes a section called the
Jitaka, which describes Buddha's birth

00:41:03.920 --> 00:41:12.160 align:start position:0%
story, and a section about tantras,
which are esoteric, or more secret

00:41:09.440 --> 00:41:17.280 align:start position:0%
practices meant only for those with
specialized knowledge. Now, as you might

00:41:14.880 --> 00:41:22.079 align:start position:0%
have guessed, the Chinese cannon is
mostly written in Chinese, classical

00:41:19.839 --> 00:41:27.760 align:start position:0%
Chinese to be exact, although the
Japanese version does include some parts

00:41:24.640 --> 00:41:33.200 align:start position:0%
in Japanese. This is why the Pali canon
is generally understood to be the older

00:41:30.160 --> 00:41:38.960 align:start position:0%
of the two cannons. After all, Pali is
an ancient Indian language and India is

00:41:36.000 --> 00:41:43.040 align:start position:0%
where Buddhism originated. However, this
paints a bit of a wrong picture. It's

00:41:41.200 --> 00:41:48.720 align:start position:0%
actually more accurate to say that the
polycanon is the oldest complete version

00:41:46.240 --> 00:41:53.040 align:start position:0%
of the Buddhist scriptures. This is
because there are in fact parts of the

00:41:50.400 --> 00:41:57.839 align:start position:0%
Chinese cannon for which we do have the
corresponding much older Sanskrit

00:41:55.440 --> 00:42:04.000 align:start position:0%
versions. It's just that we don't have
the complete Chinese cannon available in

00:42:00.880 --> 00:42:08.640 align:start position:0%
Sanskrit. Okay. Now before I move on, I
want to briefly describe the main

00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:13.920 align:start position:0%
difference between Thera Buddhism and
Mahayana Buddhism in terms of beliefs.

00:42:11.680 --> 00:42:18.960 align:start position:0%
In both cases, the ultimate goal is to
achieve enlightenment, which then frees

00:42:16.480 --> 00:42:23.839 align:start position:0%
a person from the continuous cycle of
birth, death, and rebirth, [snorts]

00:42:21.119 --> 00:42:29.920 align:start position:0%
which by the way is also the goal in
Hinduism. Thevada Buddhists teach that

00:42:26.960 --> 00:42:35.680 align:start position:0%
there are three paths to enlightenment.
The first and by far the most common

00:42:32.560 --> 00:42:41.200 align:start position:0%
path is the student path in which a
person learns from the teachings of a

00:42:38.000 --> 00:42:46.960 align:start position:0%
Buddha and eventually becomes an arhat
mostly by means of strict discipline.

00:42:44.400 --> 00:42:52.480 align:start position:0%
Once a person becomes an arhat they will
no longer be reborn. The second path is

00:42:49.680 --> 00:42:57.440 align:start position:0%
that of the solitary Buddha in which a
person achieves enlightenment on their

00:42:54.560 --> 00:43:02.800 align:start position:0%
own but is unable to teach others how to
do it. Finally, there is the full Buddha

00:43:00.560 --> 00:43:08.560 align:start position:0%
path in which a person achieves
enlightenment on their own and is also

00:43:05.839 --> 00:43:13.680 align:start position:0%
able to teach others how to reach it.
This obviously was the path taken by

00:43:10.720 --> 00:43:20.480 align:start position:0%
Sedartha Gota which is why he is called
the Buddha. Now what a lot of non

00:43:16.720 --> 00:43:26.640 align:start position:0%
Buddhists don't know is that the Buddha
was not the only person to achieve full

00:43:23.280 --> 00:43:32.400 align:start position:0%
Buddhahood. The polycanon mentions 27
Buddhas by name. Buddhas who lived

00:43:28.880 --> 00:43:38.240 align:start position:0%
before the Buddha. The three most recent
being Kakusandanda, Konagamana and

00:43:35.599 --> 00:43:44.800 align:start position:0%
Kasaba. It also talks about a future
Buddha named Maitraa. Which brings me to

00:43:41.440 --> 00:43:51.040 align:start position:0%
the word bodhicattva which is a term
that is used to refer to someone on the

00:43:47.760 --> 00:43:56.480 align:start position:0%
path towards becoming a full Buddha. In
Theraoda Buddhism, bodhicattvas are

00:43:53.760 --> 00:44:01.520 align:start position:0%
thought to be rare with Maitraa being
the only current one. Like I say, in

00:43:59.119 --> 00:44:08.400 align:start position:0%
Thera Buddhism, most people take the
Arhat path. And this is where Mahayana

00:44:05.040 --> 00:44:14.079 align:start position:0%
Buddhism is very different. In Mahayana
Buddhism, the first two paths are viewed

00:44:10.800 --> 00:44:20.880 align:start position:0%
as being very much inferior. This is why
Mahayana Buddhists refer to Thera as

00:44:17.440 --> 00:44:26.720 align:start position:0%
Hinayana which means the lesser path. In
contrast, the word Mahayana means the

00:44:23.599 --> 00:44:33.040 align:start position:0%
greater path. Mahayana teaches that the
full Buddha path also known as the

00:44:29.440 --> 00:44:38.319 align:start position:0%
bodhicattva path is open to everyone. It
sees bodhicattvas as being compassionate

00:44:35.760 --> 00:44:42.720 align:start position:0%
individuals who put off enlightenment
for the sake of helping others.

00:44:40.240 --> 00:44:48.000 align:start position:0%
Therefore, in Mahayana Buddhism, there
are lots of bodhicattvas, many of whom

00:44:45.839 --> 00:44:53.359 align:start position:0%
are understood to be residing in higher
realms. So, Mahayana Buddhists often

00:44:50.960 --> 00:44:58.000 align:start position:0%
pray to bodhicattvas and ask them for
help. One example of a bodhicattva is

00:44:56.000 --> 00:45:04.000 align:start position:0%
this guy, often called the laughing
Buddha or fat Buddha. His real name is

00:45:00.720 --> 00:45:08.640 align:start position:0%
actually Budet and he was a monk who
lived around a thousand years ago. But

00:45:06.000 --> 00:45:13.920 align:start position:0%
here's the important thing. Buddha and
the Buddha are not the same person. The

00:45:11.200 --> 00:45:20.160 align:start position:0%
Buddha is Sedartha Gotimma, the founder
of Buddhism, who became a Buddha over

00:45:16.560 --> 00:45:26.640 align:start position:0%
2,000 years ago. In contrast, Buddh is a
bodhicattva on his way to becoming a

00:45:23.200 --> 00:45:30.880 align:start position:0%
Buddha. Some think that he is Maitraa,
that future Buddha that I mentioned

00:45:28.400 --> 00:45:35.760 align:start position:0%
earlier. All of this brings up the
question, are there gods in Buddhism?

00:45:34.000 --> 00:45:40.560 align:start position:0%
Well, it kind of depends on your
definition of a god. Although Buddhism

00:45:38.400 --> 00:45:45.920 align:start position:0%
is often said to be an atheistic
religion in Mahayana Buddhism at least,

00:45:43.520 --> 00:45:51.119 align:start position:0%
a bodhicattva certainly seems to be
something a little bit similar to a god.

00:45:48.480 --> 00:45:57.599 align:start position:0%
Maybe not the omnipotent sort of god
that Abrahamic religions talk about, but

00:45:54.319 --> 00:46:04.720 align:start position:0%
some sort of spiritual being for sure.
In thevada Buddhism, this is less true.

00:46:01.839 --> 00:46:09.599 align:start position:0%
For example, you might see a Thera
Buddhist standing in front of a statue

00:46:07.119 --> 00:46:14.079 align:start position:0%
of the Buddha with their hands together.
But in this case, they are not actually

00:46:11.680 --> 00:46:19.359 align:start position:0%
worshiping Buddha as a god. Instead,
they are simply showing respect or using

00:46:17.040 --> 00:46:24.480 align:start position:0%
the Buddha's form as an aid to
meditation. Okay, let's now go back to

00:46:21.920 --> 00:46:29.920 align:start position:0%
the family tree chart. There are three
particular subbranches of East Asian

00:46:27.119 --> 00:46:35.040 align:start position:0%
Mahayana that I'd like to point out.
There are actually many more than these,

00:46:32.560 --> 00:46:42.000 align:start position:0%
but these three tend to be the most
popular. The first is Chan Buddhism,

00:46:38.319 --> 00:46:48.400 align:start position:0%
known as Zen Buddhism in Japan. It is
particularly popular in the West and

00:46:45.520 --> 00:46:53.440 align:start position:0%
mostly focused on meditation. Then
there's pure land Buddhism where the

00:46:51.040 --> 00:46:58.800 align:start position:0%
focus is trying to get reborn in a
special purified land where it's then

00:46:56.319 --> 00:47:04.480 align:start position:0%
easier to achieve enlightenment. The
most popular pure land in pure land

00:47:01.760 --> 00:47:11.599 align:start position:0%
Buddhism is the one formed by a Buddha
named Amitaba. Finally, there's Tianti,

00:47:07.839 --> 00:47:16.480 align:start position:0%
known as Tendai in Japan and Chiante in
Korea. It focuses on the Lotus Sutra

00:47:14.720 --> 00:47:22.000 align:start position:0%
that I mentioned earlier, which teaches
that all paths eventually lead to the

00:47:19.200 --> 00:47:26.880 align:start position:0%
one bodhicattva path. Okay. I now want
to turn our attention to Tibetan

00:47:24.480 --> 00:47:32.400 align:start position:0%
Buddhism. Back in the early days of
Mahayana, there was another movement

00:47:29.040 --> 00:47:37.119 align:start position:0%
that split off known as Vajraana. But
like Mahayana, this was not a separate

00:47:35.040 --> 00:47:42.720 align:start position:0%
school of Buddhism, but rather a
movement that impacted several schools.

00:47:39.760 --> 00:47:48.480 align:start position:0%
One school that took on Vajraana ideas
was the Moola Sarvastiv School, which

00:47:45.920 --> 00:47:55.280 align:start position:0%
was probably a branch of the similarly
named Sarvastiv School. It eventually

00:47:51.760 --> 00:48:00.160 align:start position:0%
spread north to Tibet and Bhutan which
is where it is mostly found today.

00:47:57.760 --> 00:48:05.440 align:start position:0%
Tibetan Buddhism differs from other
forms of Buddhism in that it

00:48:02.400 --> 00:48:10.880 align:start position:0%
incorporates far more esoteric practices
such as chanting, reciting incantations

00:48:08.800 --> 00:48:15.680 align:start position:0%
and making geometric patterns called
mandelas to help induce transances. The

00:48:13.920 --> 00:48:19.920 align:start position:0%
most famous Tibetan Buddhist is of
course the Dalai Lama who is seen as

00:48:18.000 --> 00:48:24.000 align:start position:0%
being a sort of figurehead for the
Tibetan people. He is actually the

00:48:21.839 --> 00:48:28.480 align:start position:0%
leader of just one sect of Tibetan
Buddhism of which there are currently

00:48:25.760 --> 00:48:33.839 align:start position:0%
four. However, his sect known as the
Galug or Yellow Hat school is the

00:48:31.200 --> 00:48:39.040 align:start position:0%
largest one. He is referred to as the
14th Dalai Lama because the belief is

00:48:36.559 --> 00:48:45.760 align:start position:0%
that he is the reincarnation of a man
named Geddon Dupa who died in 1474 but

00:48:43.040 --> 00:48:51.200 align:start position:0%
continues to be reborn on earth. In
turn, all of the Dalai Lamas are said to

00:48:48.079 --> 00:48:58.240 align:start position:0%
be incarnations of a bodhicattva called
Ava Loki Tasvara. Now before I go I want

00:48:54.960 --> 00:49:02.880 align:start position:0%
to briefly mention Janism which is the
other religion that can be traced back

00:49:00.319 --> 00:49:08.160 align:start position:0%
to the shana movement. It was founded by
a man named Mahaviraa who as you can see

00:49:05.680 --> 00:49:13.599 align:start position:0%
here is often depicted as looking quite
similar to the Buddha. In fact the two

00:49:10.720 --> 00:49:18.559 align:start position:0%
teachers lived around the same time with
Mahaviraa being the older of the two

00:49:16.240 --> 00:49:24.079 align:start position:0%
whereas the Buddha was born in Casala.
Mahaviraa was born in Vrigi. One of the

00:49:21.520 --> 00:49:30.160 align:start position:0%
key features of the Jane religion is
nonviolence and therefore most Janes are

00:49:26.880 --> 00:49:34.880 align:start position:0%
vegetarians. Today Janism is much
smaller than Buddhism and really there

00:49:32.160 --> 00:49:41.599 align:start position:0%
are only two main branches. The larger
one is called civara which means white

00:49:38.240 --> 00:49:47.119 align:start position:0%
clad because its monks wear white robes.
Note the face mask also. Janes have been

00:49:44.559 --> 00:49:52.319 align:start position:0%
wearing face masks long before the
current pandemic. This helps prevent

00:49:49.599 --> 00:49:57.680 align:start position:0%
sacred items from being contaminated.
The other branch of Janism is called

00:49:54.480 --> 00:50:02.559 align:start position:0%
dumbbara, meaning skyclad. This is
because the male monks in this sect wear

00:50:00.160 --> 00:50:09.240 align:start position:0%
no clothes at all. A testament to the
fact that they want as few earthly

00:50:05.280 --> 00:50:09.240 align:start position:0%
possessions as possible.

00:50:09.759 --> 00:50:18.079 align:start position:0%
[music]
Okay. So sikism traces its origins to a

00:50:14.240 --> 00:50:23.359 align:start position:0%
man named Nanuk who was born in 1469 in
what is today Pakistan. However, more

00:50:20.720 --> 00:50:28.800 align:start position:0%
importantly he was born in the region of
Punjab which is located on both sides of

00:50:26.400 --> 00:50:33.920 align:start position:0%
the Pakistan India border. The word
Punjab literally means five rivers and

00:50:31.760 --> 00:50:38.400 align:start position:0%
for most of its history it was not split
down the middle like it is today. For

00:50:36.000 --> 00:50:43.520 align:start position:0%
example, when Nanuk was born, it was a
single province of the Delhi Sultanate,

00:50:41.040 --> 00:50:48.640 align:start position:0%
the first major Muslim state in South
Asia. This is important because while

00:50:45.920 --> 00:50:53.119 align:start position:0%
Nanuk was born into a Hindu family, he
lived in a society that also included

00:50:50.720 --> 00:50:56.960 align:start position:0%
many Muslims. He thus became very
familiar with [clears throat] both

00:50:54.240 --> 00:51:02.319 align:start position:0%
religions. As the story goes, one day
around the age of 33, Nanuk went missing

00:51:00.160 --> 00:51:07.440 align:start position:0%
while having a bath in the river. The
assumption was that he had drowned. But

00:51:04.480 --> 00:51:11.359 align:start position:0%
then after 3 days he reappeared
apparently having had some sort of

00:51:09.359 --> 00:51:17.040 align:start position:0%
spiritual experience. The first thing he
said was there is no Hindu there is no

00:51:14.079 --> 00:51:21.280 align:start position:0%
Muslim. After that Nanuk quit his job
and for about the next 20 years he

00:51:19.280 --> 00:51:26.480 align:start position:0%
traveled extensively throughout the
Indian subcontinent and West Asia as a

00:51:23.839 --> 00:51:31.920 align:start position:0%
guru teaching and gathering followers.
While traveling he composed hundreds of

00:51:29.200 --> 00:51:37.200 align:start position:0%
spiritual poems designed to be set to
music. These teachings are best

00:51:34.000 --> 00:51:42.240 align:start position:0%
summarized in the mu m which is a set of
verses that can be found on the first

00:51:39.119 --> 00:51:47.599 align:start position:0%
page of the guru grant sahib the sick
scriptures. In English it goes something

00:51:44.559 --> 00:51:53.440 align:start position:0%
like this. There is only one god. The
name of god is truth. God is creator

00:51:50.880 --> 00:51:59.040 align:start position:0%
without fear without hate. Immortal and
formless beyond birth and death

00:51:56.160 --> 00:52:05.040 align:start position:0%
self-existing realized by the grace of
the guru. After finishing his travels,

00:52:01.680 --> 00:52:10.000 align:start position:0%
Guru Nanak settled back in Punjab where
he lived until age 70. By this point,

00:52:07.599 --> 00:52:16.880 align:start position:0%
Punjab was now a part of the Mughal
Empire. Now, Guru Nanak did have two

00:52:12.800 --> 00:52:21.520 align:start position:0%
sons, Baba Shri Chand and Lakmi Das, but
neither one became his spiritual

00:52:18.720 --> 00:52:26.480 align:start position:0%
successor because Shri Chan became an
aesthetic, founding his own sect and

00:52:24.079 --> 00:52:31.839 align:start position:0%
Lakmi, well, he was considered too
materialistic. So instead before his

00:52:28.960 --> 00:52:36.960 align:start position:0%
death, Guru Nanak appointed one of his
followers named Angud to become the next

00:52:34.400 --> 00:52:41.760 align:start position:0%
guru. Now while Guru Nanak is considered
to have been a guru since birth,

00:52:39.040 --> 00:52:46.480 align:start position:0%
subsequent sik gurus are considered to
have become guru only upon the death of

00:52:44.079 --> 00:52:51.839 align:start position:0%
the previous guru. So take note that the
dates shown on the chart for guru angad

00:52:49.440 --> 00:52:58.640 align:start position:0%
as well as the rest of the gurus are not
birth to death dates but rather guru

00:52:54.720 --> 00:53:04.960 align:start position:0%
ship start to guru ship end dates. Okay.
So guru ang is important because it was

00:53:01.680 --> 00:53:11.200 align:start position:0%
he who formalized the gurmuki writing
system which is the main script used in

00:53:07.839 --> 00:53:16.240 align:start position:0%
Indian punjab today as well as by six
all over the world. Like all index

00:53:13.760 --> 00:53:21.359 align:start position:0%
scripts, it ultimately traces its
origins back to Brahmi. As you can see

00:53:18.880 --> 00:53:27.520 align:start position:0%
from our writing systems of the world
chart, his wife Ki is also notable in

00:53:24.960 --> 00:53:33.119 align:start position:0%
that it was she who established the sick
tradition of lunger. The word lunger

00:53:30.800 --> 00:53:38.880 align:start position:0%
simply means kitchen. But in the context
of sikism, it refers to a special type

00:53:35.680 --> 00:53:44.160 align:start position:0%
of community kitchen that to this day is
operated out of sick temples where

00:53:41.440 --> 00:53:49.920 align:start position:0%
anyone sick or non-sick is welcome to
come in and get a simple vegetarian meal

00:53:46.880 --> 00:53:56.160 align:start position:0%
free of charge. Now like Guru Nanak,
Guru Angod did not pass on the guru ship

00:53:53.200 --> 00:54:02.559 align:start position:0%
to one of his sons but instead before
his death at age 47 he appointed his

00:53:59.200 --> 00:54:09.440 align:start position:0%
son-in-law's uncle Ammer Das as the next
guru. Now Amar Daw was actually 73 at

00:54:05.920 --> 00:54:14.079 align:start position:0%
that point but he lived until age 95 so
was actually guru for over 20 years. He

00:54:12.160 --> 00:54:19.839 align:start position:0%
is most remembered for promoting
equality by having everyone sit and eat

00:54:16.800 --> 00:54:25.359 align:start position:0%
together during lunger regardless of sex
or class. He famously even got the

00:54:22.319 --> 00:54:30.559 align:start position:0%
Mughal emperor Akbar to do this. He was
also a vocal critic of face coverings

00:54:27.760 --> 00:54:35.359 align:start position:0%
for women and the practice of sati in
which a widow must die when her husband

00:54:32.880 --> 00:54:41.599 align:start position:0%
dies. The next sick leader was Guru
Ramdas who was married to Matabani, one

00:54:38.720 --> 00:54:46.160 align:start position:0%
of the daughters of Guru Amardas. She
was the first of four women to be given

00:54:43.440 --> 00:54:51.920 align:start position:0%
the title of Guru Mahal which basically
means consort of the guru. The three

00:54:48.880 --> 00:54:56.319 align:start position:0%
other women were Mataganga, Matakrishna
Kor and Matag Gujri. Now the most

00:54:54.800 --> 00:55:02.000 align:start position:0%
important thing to know about Guru
Ramdas is that it was he who founded the

00:54:59.200 --> 00:55:07.760 align:start position:0%
city of Amritzar which became the
cultural and spiritual center of Sikism.

00:55:04.880 --> 00:55:12.160 align:start position:0%
Its name means pool of immortality
because its central feature is this

00:55:09.599 --> 00:55:17.920 align:start position:0%
man-made lake. next to which the famous
golden temple the holiest site in

00:55:14.240 --> 00:55:23.200 align:start position:0%
Sikkism is located. Now from Guru Ramdas
onwards there was a major change in that

00:55:20.400 --> 00:55:27.920 align:start position:0%
the guru ship became hereditary being
passed along the male line although it

00:55:25.839 --> 00:55:33.680 align:start position:0%
was not always passed to the most senior
male. For example, Ramdas had three sons

00:55:31.520 --> 00:55:39.440 align:start position:0%
and he ended up choosing the youngest
Arj Dev to be the next guru. This

00:55:36.880 --> 00:55:45.760 align:start position:0%
actually created a schism within Sikism
with the followers of Ramdas's oldest

00:55:42.079 --> 00:55:50.960 align:start position:0%
son Priti Chand becoming known as the
Minas. Although that movement eventually

00:55:48.640 --> 00:55:56.400 align:start position:0%
died out. It was not however the first
schism because as you might remember

00:55:53.280 --> 00:56:02.079 align:start position:0%
Guru Nanak's eldest son also created his
own sect. His followers known as Udasis

00:55:59.680 --> 00:56:07.200 align:start position:0%
still exist today albeit in very small
numbers. The vast majority of six,

00:56:04.480 --> 00:56:11.760 align:start position:0%
however, followed Guru Arjandev. It was
he who built the first golden temple at

00:56:09.440 --> 00:56:16.160 align:start position:0%
Amritzer. Although, take note, it wasn't
actually gold at the time. You see,

00:56:13.839 --> 00:56:21.280 align:start position:0%
during the 1700s, the temple was
destroyed and rebuilt several times. And

00:56:18.960 --> 00:56:27.040 align:start position:0%
it wasn't until 1830 that it was
overlaid with gold. The official name

00:56:24.000 --> 00:56:31.760 align:start position:0%
for the temple is actually Harander Sib,
which simply means the house of God.

00:56:29.359 --> 00:56:37.839 align:start position:0%
Perhaps even more importantly though, it
was Guru Arjun Dev that compiled the

00:56:34.720 --> 00:56:44.400 align:start position:0%
earliest version of the Guru Grant Sahib
known as the Adig Grant. Adi meaning

00:56:41.040 --> 00:56:48.559 align:start position:0%
first and grant meaning book. He placed
the Adi Grant in the Golden Temple

00:56:46.880 --> 00:56:52.880 align:start position:0%
in6004.
Now up until this point, the Sik gurus

00:56:50.880 --> 00:56:57.760 align:start position:0%
had maintained good relations with the
Mughal emperors. However, when Akbar

00:56:55.520 --> 00:57:03.520 align:start position:0%
died and was succeeded by his son
Jihunger, things went downhill fast.

00:57:00.640 --> 00:57:09.280 align:start position:0%
In6006, the new emperor had Guru
Arjanddev executed, making Arjun DeDev

00:57:06.480 --> 00:57:14.240 align:start position:0%
the first sick martyr. Why this occurred
is a matter of debate. According to the

00:57:11.839 --> 00:57:19.040 align:start position:0%
traditional sick account, sikism was
growing fast at this point, causing the

00:57:16.319 --> 00:57:24.480 align:start position:0%
Mughals to see it as a threat. Also,
Jihunger supposedly considered some of

00:57:21.359 --> 00:57:29.119 align:start position:0%
the verses in the new Adi Grant to be
blasphemous. The other theory is that

00:57:26.880 --> 00:57:33.680 align:start position:0%
the execution really just had to do with
local politics. And by this point, the

00:57:31.760 --> 00:57:38.799 align:start position:0%
six weren't really considered to be much
of a threat. Either way,606 ended up

00:57:36.720 --> 00:57:44.319 align:start position:0%
being a major turning point in sick
history. This is because when Arjandev's

00:57:41.520 --> 00:57:49.280 align:start position:0%
only son Harobind became the next guru,
he transformed the role of guru into

00:57:46.559 --> 00:57:54.160 align:start position:0%
that of a secular leader in addition to
a spiritual leader. In order to

00:57:51.200 --> 00:57:59.680 align:start position:0%
symbolize this, he carried two swords,
one representing meri or his political

00:57:57.520 --> 00:58:05.440 align:start position:0%
authority and the other representing
piri, his spiritual authority. He also

00:58:02.960 --> 00:58:10.319 align:start position:0%
militarized the six so that they could
defend themselves. During his lifetime,

00:58:07.520 --> 00:58:14.319 align:start position:0%
he fought at least five major defensive
battles against the Mughals, winning

00:58:12.400 --> 00:58:19.520 align:start position:0%
them all. These took place during the
reign of Emperor Sha Jahan, who is the

00:58:17.280 --> 00:58:24.880 align:start position:0%
one who built the Taj Mahal. Guru
Harabind was predeceased by his

00:58:21.920 --> 00:58:30.480 align:start position:0%
firstborn son, Baba Gerarda, and
therefore he chose as the next guru one

00:58:27.200 --> 00:58:35.520 align:start position:0%
of his grandsons named Hart Ry. Guru
Hart Rai is sometimes called the green

00:58:33.040 --> 00:58:40.960 align:start position:0%
guru because he showed a particular
interest in environmental protection,

00:58:38.160 --> 00:58:46.000 align:start position:0%
medicinal plants and animal welfare.
During his tenure, he gave assistance to

00:58:43.440 --> 00:58:51.280 align:start position:0%
Prince Dar Shiko who was fighting with
his brothers including Arange over who

00:58:48.960 --> 00:58:56.640 align:start position:0%
would become the next Mughal Emperor. In
the end, Arangz won and therefore when

00:58:53.920 --> 00:59:03.599 align:start position:0%
he became emperor, he summoned the guru
to answer for his supposed treason. Guru

00:58:59.599 --> 00:59:08.640 align:start position:0%
Harry sent his eldest son Ramry as his
representative and in order to appease

00:59:05.839 --> 00:59:14.559 align:start position:0%
the new emperor Ramry agreed to change a
verse in the Adi Grant that Aringseeb

00:59:11.760 --> 00:59:20.960 align:start position:0%
considered to be anti-Islam. However,
his father Guru Huray was not happy with

00:59:18.319 --> 00:59:26.079 align:start position:0%
this and therefore he excommunicated
Ramry meaning that he basically banned

00:59:23.359 --> 00:59:30.160 align:start position:0%
Ramry from the sick community. Ramry
eventually became friends with the

00:59:27.760 --> 00:59:36.079 align:start position:0%
emperor and went on to establish his own
sect. The excommunication became

00:59:33.119 --> 00:59:42.799 align:start position:0%
important though because Guru Harai died
shortly thereafter at age 31 resulting

00:59:39.119 --> 00:59:51.760 align:start position:0%
in his younger son Har Krishnan becoming
the next guru at age 5. However, Guru

00:59:47.839 --> 00:59:58.079 align:start position:0%
Har Krishnan also died just a few years
later from smallpox at age seven. But

00:59:55.440 --> 01:00:03.599 align:start position:0%
before he did, he indicated that the
next guru would be found in the town of

01:00:01.040 --> 01:00:10.559 align:start position:0%
Bakala. This ended up being one of his
father's uncles, Teh Bahadur. Like Guru

01:00:07.520 --> 01:00:15.280 align:start position:0%
Nanak, Guru Teahadur
undertook several extensive voyages

01:00:12.880 --> 01:00:20.559 align:start position:0%
across the Indian subcontinent, sharing
sick teachings wherever he went.

01:00:17.520 --> 01:00:25.440 align:start position:0%
However, one day while back in Punjab,
he was asked by a group of Hindus for

01:00:23.040 --> 01:00:30.720 align:start position:0%
assistance as they were being persecuted
by the Mughal authorities. He agreed to

01:00:28.240 --> 01:00:36.880 align:start position:0%
help and for this reason was arrested
and then executed in Delhi on the orders

01:00:33.359 --> 01:00:42.480 align:start position:0%
of Emperor Arange. He thus became the
second guru to be killed by the Mughals.

01:00:40.079 --> 01:00:48.720 align:start position:0%
What followed was yet another period of
war between the six and the Mughals with

01:00:45.680 --> 01:00:55.440 align:start position:0%
the next guru being Gobend Singh the
only son of Teh Bahhatur. He fought many

01:00:52.480 --> 01:01:01.280 align:start position:0%
battles but also laid the groundwork for
how Sikism is followed today. Most

01:00:58.480 --> 01:01:07.760 align:start position:0%
importantly in 1699
he founded the Kalsa which means the

01:01:04.319 --> 01:01:12.559 align:start position:0%
pure. In a broad sense, the kalsa can
refer to the entirety of the sick

01:01:10.319 --> 01:01:18.000 align:start position:0%
community. However, in a more narrow
sense, it only refers to those either

01:01:15.359 --> 01:01:23.520 align:start position:0%
male or female who have chosen to take
some extra steps. These include a

01:01:20.720 --> 01:01:30.000 align:start position:0%
special baptism, taking the name sing
for males or cur for females, avoiding

01:01:27.440 --> 01:01:37.520 align:start position:0%
things like smoking and drinking, and
the most physical aspect, agreeing to

01:01:32.480 --> 01:01:45.280 align:start position:0%
wear the 5ks. These are k meaning uncut
hair which is why male kulsaixs wear

01:01:40.720 --> 01:01:51.920 align:start position:0%
turbons. Kanga a small wooden comb. Kura
an iron bracelet worn on the wrist.

01:01:47.760 --> 01:02:01.359 align:start position:0%
Kachera special undergarments and kerpan
a small blade. Now Guru Gobin Singh had

01:01:55.599 --> 01:02:08.400 align:start position:0%
four sons. Ajit, Jar, Zorowara and Fate.
Collectively they are known as the char

01:02:04.240 --> 01:02:14.160 align:start position:0%
sahib zade which just means four sons.
They are deeply revered in sikism

01:02:11.200 --> 01:02:21.760 align:start position:0%
because all four became martyrs at young
ages. The first two died in the battle

01:02:16.640 --> 01:02:26.799 align:start position:0%
of Chamur in 1704 at ages 17 and 13 with
the other two aged 9 and six being

01:02:24.559 --> 01:02:31.680 align:start position:0%
captured shortly thereafter and killed
on the orders of the local Mughal

01:02:28.799 --> 01:02:36.640 align:start position:0%
governor. Their grandmother Mata Gurri
was captured at the same time and died

01:02:33.760 --> 01:02:41.440 align:start position:0%
in captivity the same day. Now this
tragedy had a profound impact on sikism

01:02:39.680 --> 01:02:47.119 align:start position:0%
because it strengthened the sick
community and its resolve. But it also

01:02:44.240 --> 01:02:53.520 align:start position:0%
brought an end to the hereditary line of
gurus. You see, just before his death,

01:02:49.839 --> 01:02:58.559 align:start position:0%
Guru Goben Singh declared that the six
no longer needed a human guru because

01:02:56.000 --> 01:03:04.799 align:start position:0%
they now had each other as well as the
guru grunt sahib which he had compiled

01:03:01.680 --> 01:03:11.839 align:start position:0%
by expanding the earlier adigrant. Thus,
the gurug grant sahib became the 11th

01:03:08.160 --> 01:03:18.079 align:start position:0%
and eternal guru. Today, every sik
temple known as a gerdoara has a copy of

01:03:15.200 --> 01:03:23.039 align:start position:0%
the guru grant sahib sitting on top of a
raised platform where it is covered when

01:03:20.640 --> 01:03:28.960 align:start position:0%
not being used. During services, the
guru grant sahib is unwrapped and read

01:03:25.680 --> 01:03:33.520 align:start position:0%
from either with or without music. Now,
at this point, I want to tell you a bit

01:03:30.880 --> 01:03:38.640 align:start position:0%
about the composition of the guru grunt
sahib. It is always printed on exactly

01:03:36.799 --> 01:03:44.960 align:start position:0%
1,430
pages called an overall its content is

01:03:42.880 --> 01:03:50.240 align:start position:0%
about half the size of the Christian
Bible and about five times as long as

01:03:47.760 --> 01:03:56.240 align:start position:0%
the Quran. It is divided into three
parts. An introductory section, the main

01:03:53.359 --> 01:04:03.119 align:start position:0%
section and a concluding section. The
main section is divided into 31 primary

01:03:59.280 --> 01:04:08.400 align:start position:0%
rocks or musical colorings which are
sort of like scales in western music

01:04:06.160 --> 01:04:13.839 align:start position:0%
except that they are much more than just
that. Within each rag there are many

01:04:10.960 --> 01:04:19.920 align:start position:0%
hymns and when taken together the total
ends up being 5,894.

01:04:17.920 --> 01:04:24.799 align:start position:0%
Now, while most of these hymns were
written by sik gurus, there are also

01:04:22.640 --> 01:04:30.079 align:start position:0%
some by various Hindu and Muslim
mystics. Of the 10 sick gurus that we

01:04:27.680 --> 01:04:37.440 align:start position:0%
talked about in this video, only six
contributed hymns to the guru grant

01:04:32.079 --> 01:04:44.960 align:start position:0%
sahib. Guru Arjan wrote the most at 2218
followed by Guru Nanak with 974, Guru

01:04:41.119 --> 01:04:54.880 align:start position:0%
Amar Das with 9007, Guru Ramdas with
679, Guru Tag Bahador with 116, and Guru

01:04:51.119 --> 01:05:01.280 align:start position:0%
Ang with 62. The person with the most
hymns in the guru grand sahib who was

01:04:57.680 --> 01:05:08.240 align:start position:0%
not a sik is Kabir a Hindu mystic who
lived about a generation or so before

01:05:03.760 --> 01:05:11.240 align:start position:0%
guru nanic. He wrote a total of 541
hymns.

01:05:11.704 --> 01:05:17.839 align:start position:0%
[music]
Like I said earlier, religion in China

01:05:15.280 --> 01:05:22.799 align:start position:0%
is complicated because people there
often mix and match from more than one

01:05:20.480 --> 01:05:26.720 align:start position:0%
religious tradition. However, there are
three traditions that are the most

01:05:24.799 --> 01:05:33.200 align:start position:0%
important and these are often referred
to as the three teachings. They are

01:05:30.160 --> 01:05:38.400 align:start position:0%
Mahayana Buddhism, Dowoism, and
Confucianism. I've already talked about

01:05:35.520 --> 01:05:43.359 align:start position:0%
Mahayana Buddhism in the Buddhism video.
So, let me tell you about the other two.

01:05:41.200 --> 01:05:48.160 align:start position:0%
To do so, let me start with the earliest
form of religion to develop in China,

01:05:45.680 --> 01:05:53.280 align:start position:0%
polytheism. The symbol you see here is
from China's oldest writing system

01:05:50.319 --> 01:05:58.960 align:start position:0%
called the oracle bone script which was
used during the Shang dynasty. It's

01:05:55.680 --> 01:06:04.000 align:start position:0%
pronounced Shangd and basically means
highest god. Later this god would become

01:06:01.839 --> 01:06:10.000 align:start position:0%
associated with a figure known as the
jade emperor. Although in other contexts

01:06:06.960 --> 01:06:16.559 align:start position:0%
he is said to manifest himself as five
deities each associated with a color

01:06:13.039 --> 01:06:23.440 align:start position:0%
element, direction and planet. But Shang
D was not and is not the only Chinese

01:06:20.319 --> 01:06:29.280 align:start position:0%
god. There are dozens more such as the
dragon god who controls the rain and Xi

01:06:26.400 --> 01:06:34.799 align:start position:0%
Wong Mu, the queen mother of the west
who is associated with death and has the

01:06:31.599 --> 01:06:40.160 align:start position:0%
ability to bestow immortality. However,
one aspect of Chinese polytheism which

01:06:37.680 --> 01:06:45.359 align:start position:0%
developed early on is that the worship
or veneration of deceased ancestors

01:06:43.039 --> 01:06:50.000 align:start position:0%
became just as important if not more
important than the worship of deities.

01:06:47.920 --> 01:06:55.280 align:start position:0%
Another group of spiritual beings called
immortals became important as well.

01:06:52.640 --> 01:07:01.440 align:start position:0%
Immortals are former humans who are not
quite gods but who live on after death

01:06:58.319 --> 01:07:06.880 align:start position:0%
and can possess great powers. Thus, as
time went on, self-ultivation in this

01:07:04.319 --> 01:07:13.119 align:start position:0%
life became more and more important in
Chinese religion. Then, during the 500s

01:07:10.480 --> 01:07:18.559 align:start position:0%
B.C.E., there was an explosion of new
ideas in China, which resulted in what's

01:07:15.440 --> 01:07:22.240 align:start position:0%
called the 100 schools of thought. Most
of these schools eventually went

01:07:20.160 --> 01:07:27.440 align:start position:0%
extinct, but there are two that have
survived all the way to today. These

01:07:24.640 --> 01:07:31.920 align:start position:0%
are, as I'm sure you've guessed, Dowoism
and Confucianism.

01:07:29.520 --> 01:07:36.559 align:start position:0%
Daoism is the more mystical and
spiritual of the two. It incorporates

01:07:34.319 --> 01:07:41.760 align:start position:0%
all of the gods and immortals from
Chinese polytheism, but also places a

01:07:39.280 --> 01:07:46.000 align:start position:0%
strong emphasis on living in harmony
with something called thao, a word

01:07:43.760 --> 01:07:51.039 align:start position:0%
that's kind of hard to define quickly in
English. On a basic level, it simply

01:07:48.319 --> 01:07:55.599 align:start position:0%
means way or path. But on a deeper
level, it refers to the universe's

01:07:53.119 --> 01:08:01.119 align:start position:0%
ultimate reality. It is usually
associated with the complimentary forces

01:07:58.319 --> 01:08:06.079 align:start position:0%
yin and yang which you probably know
about because of this symbol.

01:08:03.599 --> 01:08:10.480 align:start position:0%
Confucianism on the other hand is more
focused on the physical world and on

01:08:08.799 --> 01:08:14.559 align:start position:0%
practical matters such as good
government as well as social harmony

01:08:12.480 --> 01:08:20.960 align:start position:0%
whether it's at the family level or the
national level. This is why Confucianism

01:08:17.520 --> 01:08:26.480 align:start position:0%
is often said to be more of a philosophy
than a religion. It's named after its

01:08:23.759 --> 01:08:31.839 align:start position:0%
founder, Confucious, who lived around
the same time as the Buddha. Note that

01:08:28.880 --> 01:08:38.000 align:start position:0%
Confucious is the anglicized version of
Kong Fuzi, which simply means master

01:08:34.719 --> 01:08:42.640 align:start position:0%
Kong. The traditional founder of Daoism,
Laoi, is said to have lived around the

01:08:40.400 --> 01:08:46.960 align:start position:0%
same time as Confucious, and as his
elder is thought to have had some

01:08:44.400 --> 01:08:51.199 align:start position:0%
influence on him. However, nowadays, Lao
Zi is generally considered to have been

01:08:48.880 --> 01:08:55.759 align:start position:0%
more of a legendary figure, whereas
Confucious was almost certainly

01:08:53.600 --> 01:09:01.359 align:start position:0%
historical. So, like I say, a lot of
people in China follow traditions and

01:08:58.000 --> 01:09:06.960 align:start position:0%
principles associated with both Daoism
and Confucianism as well as Buddhism.

01:09:04.560 --> 01:09:12.080 align:start position:0%
So, it's not uncommon to see depictions
of the Buddha or various bodhicattvas

01:09:10.000 --> 01:09:17.759 align:start position:0%
next to those of traditional Chinese
gods or immortals. And on top of all of

01:09:14.960 --> 01:09:22.080 align:start position:0%
this, the veneration of ancestors in
China remains important to this day as

01:09:19.920 --> 01:09:27.120 align:start position:0%
well. Now, before I move on, I want to
point out some more modern trends within

01:09:24.239 --> 01:09:32.319 align:start position:0%
Chinese religion. The first is Chinese
salvationist religions, which became

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:37.359 align:start position:0%
popular in the early 20th century, but
which nowadays are mostly followed in

01:09:34.159 --> 01:09:42.319 align:start position:0%
Taiwan. A good example is Yaguandanda,
which has roots that go back to imperial

01:09:39.920 --> 01:09:47.759 align:start position:0%
times, but didn't really take off until
after 1912, which is when China became a

01:09:45.359 --> 01:09:53.359 align:start position:0%
republic. At this point, it was led by a
man named Jeang Tian Ran, who managed to

01:09:51.120 --> 01:09:58.320 align:start position:0%
grow the movement to around 12 million
members. However, once the revolution

01:09:55.679 --> 01:10:04.320 align:start position:0%
started and China became communist, it
was mostly stamped out, only to gain

01:10:00.800 --> 01:10:09.040 align:start position:0%
traction again in Taiwan during the 80s.
Like most Chinese salvationist

01:10:06.080 --> 01:10:13.440 align:start position:0%
movements, Iguandanda is kind of a
simplified version of Chinese

01:10:10.880 --> 01:10:18.640 align:start position:0%
synretatism, but packaged in a way that
is more similar to say Mormonism. In

01:10:16.320 --> 01:10:23.440 align:start position:0%
other words, there's usually a revered
leader who received a revelation from

01:10:21.280 --> 01:10:27.920 align:start position:0%
God. And there's a lot of emphasis on
the need for individual salvation and

01:10:25.760 --> 01:10:33.199 align:start position:0%
for converting others to the movement.
Another good example of a Chinese

01:10:30.400 --> 01:10:39.920 align:start position:0%
salvationist religion is the more recent
Weinianism founded by Hun Yuan. And then

01:10:37.280 --> 01:10:45.360 align:start position:0%
there's Fallon Gong, which was founded
around the same time by Ling Hong Xi.

01:10:43.199 --> 01:10:50.080 align:start position:0%
It's actually not classified as a
Chinese Salvationist religion, but does

01:10:47.920 --> 01:10:55.120 align:start position:0%
share some similarities with them,
although it's more focused on doing

01:10:51.920 --> 01:11:00.080 align:start position:0%
special exercises called Chi Gong. It
has become particularly popular within

01:10:57.360 --> 01:11:04.320 align:start position:0%
the Chinese expat community in the west
where it's known for being super

01:11:01.840 --> 01:11:08.739 align:start position:0%
conservative and for protesting against
China.

01:11:06.719 --> 01:11:08.739 align:start position:0%
[music]

01:11:09.120 --> 01:11:16.960 align:start position:0%
Judaism has its roots in ancient
Israelite religion which was practiced

01:11:14.080 --> 01:11:21.280 align:start position:0%
by the kingdoms of Israel and Judah.
Israel and Judah were relatively small

01:11:19.520 --> 01:11:26.640 align:start position:0%
kingdoms, but they happened to be
located right in between two of the most

01:11:24.320 --> 01:11:31.840 align:start position:0%
important centers of civilization in the
ancient world, Egypt and Mesopotamia,

01:11:29.760 --> 01:11:36.560 align:start position:0%
which is why Egypt and then later
Assyria and Babylon played such a huge

01:11:34.560 --> 01:11:41.840 align:start position:0%
role in their history. Now, there are
two main explanations for where ancient

01:11:38.960 --> 01:11:47.440 align:start position:0%
Israelite religion came from. One of
course is that it came directly from God

01:11:44.640 --> 01:11:53.920 align:start position:0%
through divine revelation specifically
when Moses received the Torah. The other

01:11:51.040 --> 01:11:59.440 align:start position:0%
is that it developed slowly over time
based on its interactions with both

01:11:56.239 --> 01:12:04.719 align:start position:0%
Egypt and Mesopotamia. In fact, the
scholarly consensus nowadays is that the

01:12:02.159 --> 01:12:10.400 align:start position:0%
Israelites actually started out as a
subset of Canaanites and then slowly

01:12:07.520 --> 01:12:15.280 align:start position:0%
went from polytheism to monotheism over
time. Either way, what we're concerned

01:12:13.120 --> 01:12:22.080 align:start position:0%
with here is what happened during the
late Iron Age. Basically, Israel fell to

01:12:19.120 --> 01:12:27.600 align:start position:0%
the Assyrians and Judah fell to the
Babylonians. But then following a brief

01:12:24.560 --> 01:12:32.719 align:start position:0%
exile in Babylon, the former inhabitants
of Judah, now called Jews, were able to

01:12:30.560 --> 01:12:42.239 align:start position:0%
return to their land and rebuild their
temple. Which is why Judaism between 537

01:12:36.800 --> 01:12:47.600 align:start position:0%
B.CE and 70 CE is known as second temple
Judaism. During this time it was

01:12:44.640 --> 01:12:52.080 align:start position:0%
influenced by both Zoroastrianism
which was the religion of the Persians

01:12:49.760 --> 01:12:56.880 align:start position:0%
as well as by Helenism which was the
religion of the Greeks but most

01:12:53.840 --> 01:13:02.800 align:start position:0%
importantly by this point Judaism was
definitely monotheistic which is to this

01:12:59.840 --> 01:13:08.560 align:start position:0%
day its defining feature. However, by
the time that the Romans took over there

01:13:05.440 --> 01:13:14.159 align:start position:0%
were four major sects within second
temple Judaism. The Pharisees who

01:13:11.679 --> 01:13:20.480 align:start position:0%
represented the everyday people, the
Essenes who were a mystical bunch, the

01:13:17.440 --> 01:13:25.920 align:start position:0%
Zealots who wanted to fight against the
Romans, and the Sadducees who were the

01:13:23.120 --> 01:13:30.880 align:start position:0%
elites who ran the temple. To this was
added a fifth group, the early

01:13:28.560 --> 01:13:36.800 align:start position:0%
Christians. However, Christianity
quickly became a separate, mostly

01:13:33.520 --> 01:13:41.760 align:start position:0%
gentile, meaning non-Jewish religion.
The early Christians who continued to

01:13:39.120 --> 01:13:46.719 align:start position:0%
maintain Jewish traditions such as the
Ebianites and Nazarines eventually went

01:13:44.480 --> 01:13:52.560 align:start position:0%
extinct, although there is evidence that
they had an influence on the development

01:13:49.120 --> 01:13:58.880 align:start position:0%
of Islam before doing so. Anyway, the
Essenes, Zealots, and Sadducees also all

01:13:56.320 --> 01:14:05.520 align:start position:0%
went extinct back when the Romans
destroyed the Jewish temple in 70 CE.

01:14:02.719 --> 01:14:10.560 align:start position:0%
Thus, the only sect of second temple
Judaism that survived was that of the

01:14:08.080 --> 01:14:15.920 align:start position:0%
Pharisees. Now, the New Testament does
not have a lot of nice things to say

01:14:13.120 --> 01:14:21.360 align:start position:0%
about the Pharisees. But for Jews today,
the Pharisees are actually our spiritual

01:14:18.800 --> 01:14:26.400 align:start position:0%
ancestors. After the destruction of
Jerusalem, they set up a school in the

01:14:23.760 --> 01:14:31.920 align:start position:0%
nearby town of Yavnne, known in
Christian sources as Jamnia, which is

01:14:29.199 --> 01:14:36.960 align:start position:0%
where they helped Judaism evolve from
being a temple-based religion to one

01:14:34.159 --> 01:14:43.120 align:start position:0%
that is based mostly on communal prayer
and on studying the five books of Moses

01:14:40.159 --> 01:14:50.560 align:start position:0%
known as the Torah. The scholars at this
Yavn school eventually became known as

01:14:46.000 --> 01:14:56.000 align:start position:0%
rabbis. Thus, Judaism as it exists today
can more accurately be called rabbitic

01:14:53.360 --> 01:15:01.360 align:start position:0%
Judaism in order to distinguish it from
the earlier second temple Judaism. One

01:14:59.199 --> 01:15:07.440 align:start position:0%
of the things that the early rabbis did
was to develop the Talmud which actually

01:15:04.320 --> 01:15:13.040 align:start position:0%
has two components. The Mishna which was
written first and the Gamarra which was

01:15:10.080 --> 01:15:18.640 align:start position:0%
written later and consists of commentary
on the Mishna. According to tradition,

01:15:15.440 --> 01:15:23.280 align:start position:0%
the Mishna is based on the oral Torah,
which consisted of various

01:15:20.560 --> 01:15:28.400 align:start position:0%
clarifications that were given to Moses
around the same time as the written

01:15:25.520 --> 01:15:33.199 align:start position:0%
Torah. These were supposedly passed down
by word of mouth until the time of the

01:15:30.800 --> 01:15:37.760 align:start position:0%
rabbis. However, according to modern
critical scholarship, the oral Torah

01:15:35.520 --> 01:15:42.960 align:start position:0%
likely does not go all the way back to
Moses. But it does at least go back to

01:15:40.800 --> 01:15:48.080 align:start position:0%
the second temple period to figures like
Hel and Shmai who lived just prior to

01:15:45.840 --> 01:15:52.480 align:start position:0%
the time of Jesus. If you want to learn
more about the various rabbis mentioned

01:15:50.159 --> 01:15:56.880 align:start position:0%
in the Mishna, we actually have a video
on that which I'll link to in the

01:15:54.480 --> 01:16:01.840 align:start position:0%
description. Now, in case you've heard
some of the nasty things that sometimes

01:15:59.440 --> 01:16:07.120 align:start position:0%
get said about the Talmud, let me make
it clear that in those cases, the Telmud

01:16:04.480 --> 01:16:12.320 align:start position:0%
is usually being taken out of context
for anti-semitic reasons. Rather than

01:16:09.679 --> 01:16:17.760 align:start position:0%
being a list of clear-cut rules, the
Telmud and the various notes that now

01:16:15.199 --> 01:16:23.360 align:start position:0%
come with it are more like a collection
of case law in which various opinions

01:16:20.400 --> 01:16:27.920 align:start position:0%
are given in addition to opinions about
those opinions. and then opinions about

01:16:25.600 --> 01:16:33.360 align:start position:0%
the opinions about the opinions which is
why a typical Talmud page looks

01:16:30.320 --> 01:16:39.600 align:start position:0%
something like this. Now it's at this
point that I should bring up the Kite

01:16:35.840 --> 01:16:44.400 align:start position:0%
Jews. Kite Jews reject the Talmud and
therefore some people claim that the

01:16:41.360 --> 01:16:49.040 align:start position:0%
modern Kites can trace their lineage all
the way back to the Sadducees. But

01:16:46.960 --> 01:16:54.400 align:start position:0%
what's more likely is that they were
simply a group that broke away from

01:16:51.600 --> 01:17:00.800 align:start position:0%
mainstream rabbitic Judaism around the
year 800. An even earlier group to break

01:16:57.840 --> 01:17:07.920 align:start position:0%
away from or at least lose contact with
rabbitic Judaism is Beta Israel based in

01:17:04.719 --> 01:17:12.640 align:start position:0%
Ethiopia. They may go all the way back
to second temple times, but there is

01:17:10.560 --> 01:17:17.600 align:start position:0%
also evidence that they initially
maintained some contact with the early

01:17:15.120 --> 01:17:22.239 align:start position:0%
rabbis, but then for some reason that
contact was eventually severed. It

01:17:20.000 --> 01:17:27.840 align:start position:0%
wasn't actually until modern times that
Beta Israel was quote unquote

01:17:24.640 --> 01:17:34.000 align:start position:0%
rediscovered and integrated back into
mainstream Judaism. So again, I wouldn't

01:17:30.800 --> 01:17:38.960 align:start position:0%
consider beta Israel to be outside of
rabbitic Judaism, but rather to be a

01:17:36.560 --> 01:17:45.920 align:start position:0%
unique stream within it. But then
there's the Samaritans who definitely

01:17:42.159 --> 01:17:51.440 align:start position:0%
are a separate group from rabbitic Jews.
They claim to be the descendants of the

01:17:48.480 --> 01:17:57.199 align:start position:0%
northern 10 tribes of Israel. However,
according to historians, the situation

01:17:53.920 --> 01:18:02.400 align:start position:0%
is much more complicated. When Assyria
conquered Israel, some Israelites were

01:17:59.920 --> 01:18:06.960 align:start position:0%
carried away and then non-Israelites
were brought in to replace them.

01:18:04.400 --> 01:18:11.760 align:start position:0%
However, other Israelites simply moved
south to Jerusalem where they became

01:18:09.440 --> 01:18:16.960 align:start position:0%
integrated into the kingdom of Judah.
Then when the Babylonians conquered

01:18:14.159 --> 01:18:21.679 align:start position:0%
Judah, a split occurred whereby many of
the elites were carried off to Babylon,

01:18:19.440 --> 01:18:27.760 align:start position:0%
whereas the everyday people were left
behind where they sometimes intermarried

01:18:24.480 --> 01:18:32.080 align:start position:0%
with foreigners. When the Judean elites
returned to rebuild the Jerusalem

01:18:29.920 --> 01:18:37.120 align:start position:0%
temple, some of those who had been left
behind, who the Bible calls the people

01:18:34.640 --> 01:18:42.400 align:start position:0%
of the land, wanted to build a separate
temple, which they did at Mount Garazim,

01:18:40.239 --> 01:18:46.640 align:start position:0%
which happened to be in the territory
where the northern tribes used to live.

01:18:44.640 --> 01:18:53.280 align:start position:0%
So to me, it's unclear whether the
Samaritan Jewish division was more about

01:18:49.760 --> 01:18:58.560 align:start position:0%
an ethnic division or a class division.
Either way, what we do know is that the

01:18:56.000 --> 01:19:05.360 align:start position:0%
Samaritans eventually dwindled in size
and today consists of just around 850

01:19:02.560 --> 01:19:12.239 align:start position:0%
people. Okay, so let's now look at how
the main branch of rabbitic Judaism

01:19:08.480 --> 01:19:18.719 align:start position:0%
evolved. Generally speaking, from 70 CE
to around 1740 CE, there was nothing

01:19:16.080 --> 01:19:24.480 align:start position:0%
within Judaism that was anything like
what the word denomination refers to.

01:19:21.520 --> 01:19:28.960 align:start position:0%
there was simply Judaism. This is partly
because Jews were very much the minority

01:19:27.120 --> 01:19:33.920 align:start position:0%
wherever they were found. So when you're
already a small persecuted group, you

01:19:31.280 --> 01:19:39.120 align:start position:0%
tend to stick together. However, it also
boils down to the fact that Judaism to

01:19:36.159 --> 01:19:42.960 align:start position:0%
this day has no central leadership. If
you're looking for an analogy from

01:19:40.880 --> 01:19:48.640 align:start position:0%
within the Christian framework, it would
be best to say that Jews follow a

01:19:45.760 --> 01:19:54.960 align:start position:0%
congregational style of governance, sort
of like the Baptists. Rabbis get trained

01:19:51.920 --> 01:19:59.840 align:start position:0%
at rabbitical colleges where some rabbis
end up being more influential than

01:19:56.800 --> 01:20:04.560 align:start position:0%
others. But then each congregation gets
to choose who they want to be their

01:20:02.000 --> 01:20:08.880 align:start position:0%
rabbi and how they want to run things.
Although note that nowadays some

01:20:06.400 --> 01:20:13.920 align:start position:0%
countries do have what's called a chief
rabbi, which I'll get to later. Now

01:20:11.920 --> 01:20:19.679 align:start position:0%
don't get me wrong when I say that there
was just one Judaism until 1740. I'm not

01:20:17.840 --> 01:20:24.560 align:start position:0%
saying that there were absolutely no
differences to be found. There were.

01:20:22.159 --> 01:20:32.000 align:start position:0%
Which brings me to the terms Safharti,
Ashkanazi, and Misrahi. But please note

01:20:28.480 --> 01:20:37.679 align:start position:0%
these are not different denominations.
They are more like regional subcultures.

01:20:34.960 --> 01:20:42.080 align:start position:0%
To explain, let's bring up a map.
Basically, following the fall of

01:20:39.360 --> 01:20:47.440 align:start position:0%
Jerusalem, Jews ended up all over the
Roman Empire. One particular area where

01:20:44.719 --> 01:20:53.199 align:start position:0%
a lot of them ended up is in what we
today call Spain and Portugal. Jews from

01:20:50.719 --> 01:20:58.960 align:start position:0%
this area became known as Sephardic
Jews. Sepharod simply being the Hebrew

01:20:56.239 --> 01:21:03.040 align:start position:0%
word for Spain. For many centuries, they
were ruled by Muslims who generally

01:21:00.880 --> 01:21:08.719 align:start position:0%
treated them very well. However,
following the reconista and the shift

01:21:05.679 --> 01:21:13.920 align:start position:0%
back to Christian control, Jews were
expelled from the Iberian Peninsula and

01:21:11.760 --> 01:21:19.360 align:start position:0%
thus many of them ended up back in the
Middle East where they were welcomed by

01:21:16.480 --> 01:21:24.640 align:start position:0%
the Ottoman Empire. Others ended up in
North Africa or in the low countries or

01:21:22.159 --> 01:21:29.600 align:start position:0%
in the so-called new world where they
settled long before the arrival of the

01:21:26.800 --> 01:21:34.960 align:start position:0%
now more dominant Ashkanazi Jews. The
word Ashkanazi comes from the name

01:21:31.920 --> 01:21:40.560 align:start position:0%
Ashkanaz, which was a very old Jewish
name for Germany. Based on recent DNA

01:21:38.000 --> 01:21:45.920 align:start position:0%
studies, we now know a lot about the
origins of the Ashkanazi Jews. It's now

01:21:43.760 --> 01:21:51.040 align:start position:0%
thought that they originated in southern
Italy before next settling in Germany

01:21:48.640 --> 01:21:56.560 align:start position:0%
around the year 800. At some point
though, their numbers dwindled to around

01:21:53.280 --> 01:22:01.440 align:start position:0%
just 350 people, which led to what's
called a genetic bottleneck. Before this

01:21:59.520 --> 01:22:06.960 align:start position:0%
point, there was a good deal of
intermarriage with non-Jews,

01:22:04.000 --> 01:22:11.040 align:start position:0%
particularly southern Italians. But then
after this point, the group mostly

01:22:08.960 --> 01:22:16.719 align:start position:0%
intermarried amongst themselves,
resulting in the creation of a distinct

01:22:13.760 --> 01:22:22.560 align:start position:0%
ethnic group called Ashkanazi Jewish,
which has clear DNA markers that can

01:22:19.360 --> 01:22:27.760 align:start position:0%
show up on a DNA test. But take note,
even though Ashkanazi Jews are at least

01:22:25.520 --> 01:22:32.159 align:start position:0%
partially European, a good amount of
their DNA can still be traced all the

01:22:30.400 --> 01:22:38.639 align:start position:0%
way back to the Middle East,
particularly along the male only line.

01:22:35.120 --> 01:22:44.880 align:start position:0%
So the old theory that the Ashkanazi are
somehow fake Jews descended from the

01:22:41.760 --> 01:22:50.719 align:start position:0%
Khazars who merely converted to Judaism
is now known to be false. I should also

01:22:48.159 --> 01:22:55.520 align:start position:0%
note that while the Ashkenazi Jews
originally settled in Germany, most of

01:22:53.199 --> 01:23:00.880 align:start position:0%
them ended up being pushed into Eastern
Europe, which is where most of them

01:22:57.520 --> 01:23:06.639 align:start position:0%
lived until the 20th century. Okay. So
in addition to Sphartic Jews and

01:23:03.520 --> 01:23:11.520 align:start position:0%
Ashkanazi Jews, there are also Misrai
Jews, which is sort of a catch-all term

01:23:09.199 --> 01:23:17.360 align:start position:0%
for Jews that never left the Middle
East. Misrai Jews ended up assimilating

01:23:15.040 --> 01:23:22.080 align:start position:0%
a lot of Sphartic customs, though,
because remember, many Sphartic Jews

01:23:19.920 --> 01:23:28.239 align:start position:0%
ended up back in the Middle East. So
take note that nowadays the Misrais are

01:23:25.679 --> 01:23:33.360 align:start position:0%
often lumped together with the Spharti
Jews. But again, before I move on, I

01:23:30.960 --> 01:23:38.960 align:start position:0%
want to emphasize that the Safhari
versus Ashkanazi division has nothing to

01:23:36.159 --> 01:23:45.040 align:start position:0%
do with denominations nor with any
theological differences. In Judaism, we

01:23:42.480 --> 01:23:51.360 align:start position:0%
have a concept called Minhag, which can
be roughly translated as customs.

01:23:48.159 --> 01:23:56.080 align:start position:0%
Spharti Jews and Ashkanazi Jews may have
different Minhog, but they share the

01:23:53.760 --> 01:24:00.560 align:start position:0%
same religion. The best analogy from
within the Christian framework would be

01:23:58.080 --> 01:24:06.080 align:start position:0%
to compare Catholics who use the Latin
right with those who use the Syriak

01:24:03.280 --> 01:24:12.239 align:start position:0%
right. Their clothing and liturgy might
be different, but their theology is not.

01:24:09.280 --> 01:24:18.080 align:start position:0%
To this day, Ashkanazi Jews rely heavily
on philosophical works developed by

01:24:14.880 --> 01:24:22.560 align:start position:0%
Spharti Jews and vice versa. One good
example is Mymonades who I mentioned

01:24:20.639 --> 01:24:28.639 align:start position:0%
earlier as being the one who developed
the 13 principles of faith. He was

01:24:25.520 --> 01:24:34.480 align:start position:0%
Safharti but he's just as important to
Ashkanazis. In contrast, there's Rashi

01:24:31.679 --> 01:24:39.679 align:start position:0%
whose commentaries are included in all
modern editions of the Talmud. He was

01:24:36.880 --> 01:24:45.679 align:start position:0%
Ashkanazi but he is also considered
authoritative by Safhari. Now before I

01:24:42.800 --> 01:24:52.400 align:start position:0%
move on to the modern denominations of
Judaism, I want to point out a book

01:24:48.080 --> 01:24:58.400 align:start position:0%
called the Schulhan Aruk written in 1565
by the Sephardic rabbi Joseph Caro. It

01:24:55.600 --> 01:25:05.040 align:start position:0%
also contains notes by the Ashkanazi
rabbi Moses Iserles. To this day, it's

01:25:01.760 --> 01:25:10.239 align:start position:0%
kind of the authoritative text for all
things related to Jewish law. But it's

01:25:07.920 --> 01:25:15.280 align:start position:0%
important to note that it is used by
both Ashkanazi Jews and Safharti Jews.

01:25:13.440 --> 01:25:21.199 align:start position:0%
Although when it comes to Minhog or
customs, Ashkanazis follow the rulings

01:25:18.239 --> 01:25:29.520 align:start position:0%
of Rabbi Isurelus whereas Safhartis
follow the rulings of Rabbi Caro. Okay,

01:25:24.320 --> 01:25:35.679 align:start position:0%
so like I say, from 70 CE to around 1740
CE, there was pretty much just one

01:25:32.719 --> 01:25:42.000 align:start position:0%
Judaism, albeit with different customs
depending on where you lived. But from

01:25:38.239 --> 01:25:47.360 align:start position:0%
1740 onwards, this changed. Nowadays,
it's said that Judaism, particularly in

01:25:45.120 --> 01:25:53.679 align:start position:0%
Western countries, has three main
branches: reform, conservative, and

01:25:50.639 --> 01:25:59.120 align:start position:0%
orthodox. So before we continue down the
tree, I want to explain the main

01:25:55.840 --> 01:26:03.280 align:start position:0%
differences between these three branches
or as I'm calling them here,

01:26:01.679 --> 01:26:08.400 align:start position:0%
denominations.
At the end of the day, the difference

01:26:05.280 --> 01:26:14.719 align:start position:0%
boils down to just one thing and one
thing only, their approach to Jewish

01:26:11.360 --> 01:26:20.960 align:start position:0%
law, which is called halaka. Orthodox
Jews see halaka as being binding and for

01:26:18.320 --> 01:26:26.080 align:start position:0%
the most part unchanging. binding means
you have to follow it, not in order to

01:26:23.280 --> 01:26:31.280 align:start position:0%
obtain salvation, but simply because God
says so. So, Orthodox Jews followed the

01:26:28.880 --> 01:26:37.840 align:start position:0%
law very carefully in the same way that
it's been followed for over 2,000 years.

01:26:34.320 --> 01:26:44.080 align:start position:0%
In contrast, conservative Jews, known as
Mazorti Jews outside of North America,

01:26:40.560 --> 01:26:48.560 align:start position:0%
see halaka as being binding but not
unchanging. In other words, the law

01:26:46.239 --> 01:26:54.480 align:start position:0%
should evolve over time in order to keep
up with how human society has evolved.

01:26:51.520 --> 01:26:59.840 align:start position:0%
So, for example, Orthodox Jews won't
drive a car on Shabbat because both

01:26:57.120 --> 01:27:04.080 align:start position:0%
combustion engines and electric engines
involve lighting a fire. And in the

01:27:01.920 --> 01:27:09.360 align:start position:0%
Torah, lighting a fire is considered
work, and you're not supposed to work on

01:27:06.560 --> 01:27:13.280 align:start position:0%
Shabbat. However, conservative Jews have
come to the conclusion that in our

01:27:11.360 --> 01:27:18.080 align:start position:0%
modern world, being able to attend
synagogues, which are often no longer

01:27:15.760 --> 01:27:22.400 align:start position:0%
within walking distance, is more
important than following the original

01:27:19.920 --> 01:27:28.159 align:start position:0%
rule. So, conservative rabbis have
actually changed Jewish law to say that

01:27:25.120 --> 01:27:33.120 align:start position:0%
driving a car on Shabbat is permitted
for this special circumstance. They have

01:27:30.960 --> 01:27:39.120 align:start position:0%
done similar things in terms of allowing
women to become rabbis and supporting

01:27:35.760 --> 01:27:44.719 align:start position:0%
LGBT rights. Now before I move on, let
me mention the principle of picakesh

01:27:42.400 --> 01:27:49.920 align:start position:0%
which is followed by every branch of
Judaism. This law states that any other

01:27:47.440 --> 01:27:54.400 align:start position:0%
law can be broken in order to protect
the life or health of a person. So, for

01:27:52.239 --> 01:28:00.159 align:start position:0%
example, if a person has a medical
emergency on Shabbat, even the most

01:27:57.440 --> 01:28:04.560 align:start position:0%
Orthodox Jew will drive a car in order
to get that person to the hospital as

01:28:02.159 --> 01:28:09.679 align:start position:0%
fast as possible. However, there are
three exceptions. You can't murder, you

01:28:07.280 --> 01:28:16.400 align:start position:0%
can't worship idols, and you can't
commit a sexual sin. Okay. So, finally,

01:28:12.560 --> 01:28:21.360 align:start position:0%
there are reform Jews. Reformed Jews see
halaka as being neither binding nor

01:28:19.040 --> 01:28:26.480 align:start position:0%
unchanging. This means that each
individual Jew can make up their own

01:28:23.520 --> 01:28:32.400 align:start position:0%
mind about how to follow Jewish law. So,
for example, the Torah says that Jews

01:28:29.040 --> 01:28:37.760 align:start position:0%
must not eat certain shellfish such as
prawns, but it says that beef is okay.

01:28:36.000 --> 01:28:42.000 align:start position:0%
However, in today's world, due to
climate change, it can be argued that

01:28:39.760 --> 01:28:48.159 align:start position:0%
eating beef is more problematic than
eating prawns. So some reformed Jews

01:28:44.880 --> 01:28:53.520 align:start position:0%
might decide to adopt a full pescatarian
diet for ethical reasons instead of

01:28:50.880 --> 01:28:58.560 align:start position:0%
following traditional kosher rules. A
lot of reformed Jews like to focus on

01:28:55.520 --> 01:29:04.000 align:start position:0%
the phrase tikun olam which means
repairing the world and therefore they

01:29:00.719 --> 01:29:09.199 align:start position:0%
tend to prioritize ethical mitzvot over
ritual mitzvot. Now, these may seem like

01:29:07.280 --> 01:29:14.480 align:start position:0%
some pretty big differences, but
surprisingly on the surface, these three

01:29:11.600 --> 01:29:20.159 align:start position:0%
groups can often look almost the same.
The one exception to this is a subset of

01:29:17.199 --> 01:29:24.960 align:start position:0%
Orthodox Jews known as heredi or
ultraorththodox. Although, note that the

01:29:22.560 --> 01:29:30.320 align:start position:0%
term ultraorththodox is usually
considered offensive. Heredi Jews can be

01:29:27.600 --> 01:29:36.560 align:start position:0%
broken down further into
non-hasidic. I'll explain Judaism in

01:29:34.239 --> 01:29:41.679 align:start position:0%
more detail in a moment, but for now,
note that these are the Jews that tend

01:29:38.639 --> 01:29:46.800 align:start position:0%
to be Jewish in very visible ways. They
are the ones with big black hats and

01:29:44.159 --> 01:29:51.520 align:start position:0%
long side curls. Many Christians, when
forming a mental picture of what a Jew

01:29:49.360 --> 01:29:56.000 align:start position:0%
looks like, will tend to think of a
hassidic Jew. Well, I just want to

01:29:53.840 --> 01:30:00.000 align:start position:0%
caution you against that stereotype
because that would be like a Jew

01:29:57.679 --> 01:30:04.800 align:start position:0%
assuming that all Christians look like
this. Even among orthodox Jews, there

01:30:02.639 --> 01:30:09.679 align:start position:0%
are many who don't really stand out as
being Jewish in a highly visible way and

01:30:07.679 --> 01:30:16.239 align:start position:0%
are more integrated into the greater
society. These non-haredi orthodox Jews

01:30:13.120 --> 01:30:21.199 align:start position:0%
are usually called modern orthodox.
Okay, so how did all these various

01:30:18.400 --> 01:30:26.400 align:start position:0%
denominations of modern Judaism come
about? Well, let's actually start with

01:30:23.600 --> 01:30:32.320 align:start position:0%
hassidism. It was founded by the Bal
Shamtove who lived in what is today

01:30:29.120 --> 01:30:36.960 align:start position:0%
Ukraine during the 1700s which is why
I've shown the kidic movement as

01:30:34.320 --> 01:30:42.480 align:start position:0%
stemming from the Ashkanazis. However,
take note that nowadays some Safhartis

01:30:39.600 --> 01:30:47.440 align:start position:0%
have also adopted.
What a lot of non-Jews don't realize

01:30:44.480 --> 01:30:51.760 align:start position:0%
about Hassidism is that it is actually a
very mystical version of Judaism. In

01:30:50.159 --> 01:30:56.159 align:start position:0%
addition to being outwardly quite
conservative, it relies heavily on

01:30:54.080 --> 01:31:01.760 align:start position:0%
Cabala, which is a mystical school of
thought within Judaism that goes back to

01:30:58.480 --> 01:31:06.320 align:start position:0%
Isaac Laura in the 1500s and Moses
DeLeon in the 1200s and perhaps even

01:31:04.800 --> 01:31:11.520 align:start position:0%
further. The other thing you need to
know aboutism is that each kidic group

01:31:09.440 --> 01:31:16.239 align:start position:0%
is centered around a single rabbitic
dynasty that can be traced back to a

01:31:13.760 --> 01:31:21.199 align:start position:0%
specific Eastern European village. So
take for example Habad which is one of

01:31:18.560 --> 01:31:26.560 align:start position:0%
the largest and most well-known kidic
groups. It was originally based in a

01:31:24.000 --> 01:31:33.040 align:start position:0%
Russian village called Lubavich which is
why followers of Kabad are also known as

01:31:30.000 --> 01:31:39.040 align:start position:0%
Labavichers. The famous 20th century
leader of this group Mendel Schneersen

01:31:35.840 --> 01:31:45.520 align:start position:0%
was a descendant of Schneer Zulman the
founder of Kabad. However, not all

01:31:42.000 --> 01:31:51.040 align:start position:0%
Ashkenazi Jews embraced Hassidism. Those
who did not became known as mitnagdim,

01:31:48.880 --> 01:31:56.560 align:start position:0%
meaning opponents, although they would
later become known as litvaks, because a

01:31:53.920 --> 01:32:01.679 align:start position:0%
lot of them were based in Lithuania.
Around the year 1770, another major

01:31:59.280 --> 01:32:08.000 align:start position:0%
event occurred mostly among the
mitnakdom known as the hoscala or Jewish

01:32:05.360 --> 01:32:13.280 align:start position:0%
enlightenment. It stemmed from and was
very similar to the general age of

01:32:10.960 --> 01:32:18.320 align:start position:0%
enlightenment that had occurred in
Europe about a century earlier.

01:32:15.920 --> 01:32:23.520 align:start position:0%
Basically, it led to Judaism being
re-examined using the lens of modern

01:32:20.480 --> 01:32:28.719 align:start position:0%
critical scholarship. But it was not all
simply about new ideas. It was also

01:32:26.159 --> 01:32:34.400 align:start position:0%
about new freedoms. Around the same time
as the Huscala, Jewish emancipation was

01:32:32.480 --> 01:32:38.800 align:start position:0%
achieved throughout most of Europe.
meaning that for the first time, Jews

01:32:36.480 --> 01:32:43.280 align:start position:0%
were given the same legal rights as
Christians. At this point, some Jews

01:32:41.120 --> 01:32:48.719 align:start position:0%
simply became secular, whereas other
Jews, particularly in Germany, sought to

01:32:46.320 --> 01:32:54.239 align:start position:0%
reform Judaism in order to bring it up
to speed with what had been learned

01:32:50.960 --> 01:32:58.000 align:start position:0%
through science and textual criticism.
Now, for the next little while, I'm

01:32:55.840 --> 01:33:02.880 align:start position:0%
going to be talking exclusively about
the United States. That's because other

01:33:00.560 --> 01:33:07.760 align:start position:0%
than Israel, this is where most of the
world's Jews currently live. But don't

01:33:05.600 --> 01:33:12.800 align:start position:0%
worry, once I'm done, I will be talking
about Israel and other countries as

01:33:10.000 --> 01:33:18.400 align:start position:0%
well. Note that it's mostly in the US
and in some similar countries like

01:33:14.960 --> 01:33:23.840 align:start position:0%
Canada and the UK that Judaism can be
divided into various denominations. So,

01:33:21.600 --> 01:33:30.400 align:start position:0%
let's start with the migration of German
Jews to the US between 1840 and 1860.

01:33:28.080 --> 01:33:36.080 align:start position:0%
Prior to this point, most Jews in
America had actually been sphartic. But

01:33:33.440 --> 01:33:43.840 align:start position:0%
pretty soon, most Jewish congregations
were not only Ashkanazi, but they were

01:33:38.800 --> 01:33:49.440 align:start position:0%
also leaning towards reform. So in 1873,
the Union of American Hebrew

01:33:46.480 --> 01:33:54.719 align:start position:0%
Congregations was established in order
to serve as the main organization for

01:33:52.320 --> 01:34:01.199 align:start position:0%
American Jews. This was followed by the
founding of Hebrew Union College in 1875

01:33:58.480 --> 01:34:06.639 align:start position:0%
as the main rebbitical school. However,
while most American Jews were reformed

01:34:03.360 --> 01:34:12.960 align:start position:0%
at this point, some were not. Therefore,
in 1886, some more conservativeleaning

01:34:10.239 --> 01:34:19.199 align:start position:0%
rabbis broke away from Hebrew Union
College and established instead the

01:34:16.159 --> 01:34:24.320 align:start position:0%
Jewish Theological Seminary. Although
please note that these so-called

01:34:21.600 --> 01:34:29.679 align:start position:0%
conservative Jews were only conservative
in comparison to reformed Jews. In the

01:34:27.360 --> 01:34:34.560 align:start position:0%
eyes of many Eastern European Jews,
these so-called conservatives were

01:34:31.840 --> 01:34:39.440 align:start position:0%
actually quite liberal. What happened
next was that many of those Eastern

01:34:36.960 --> 01:34:46.719 align:start position:0%
European Jews ended up migrating to the
US between 1880 to 1925 due to

01:34:43.760 --> 01:34:52.239 align:start position:0%
persecution in Russia. They were even
more conservative than the conservatives

01:34:48.960 --> 01:34:58.320 align:start position:0%
and thus became known as orthodox.
Therefore, we ended up with three main

01:34:55.120 --> 01:35:04.080 align:start position:0%
denominations or branches within
American Judaism. The Union of American

01:35:01.679 --> 01:35:08.800 align:start position:0%
Hebrew Congregations ended up being the
main organization for reformed Jews,

01:35:06.800 --> 01:35:13.920 align:start position:0%
eventually changing its name to the
Union for Reformed Judaism. The United

01:35:11.679 --> 01:35:19.840 align:start position:0%
Synagogue of America, established in
1913, became the main organization for

01:35:17.199 --> 01:35:25.679 align:start position:0%
conservative Jews, although it too later
changed its name to the United Synagogue

01:35:22.639 --> 01:35:31.199 align:start position:0%
of Conservative Judaism. Finally, the
Orthodox Union, established in 1898,

01:35:28.800 --> 01:35:36.639 align:start position:0%
became the main organization for modern
Orthodox Jews. Now, even if you've never

01:35:34.159 --> 01:35:42.080 align:start position:0%
heard of any of these organizations,
you've probably seen this symbol on

01:35:39.280 --> 01:35:47.040 align:start position:0%
various food packages. It means that the
Orthodox Union has deemed that item to

01:35:44.800 --> 01:35:52.239 align:start position:0%
be kosher. I also want to point out
Agaha, which is another Orthodox

01:35:49.600 --> 01:35:58.800 align:start position:0%
organization separate from the Orthodox
Union. It consists mostly of Karedi

01:35:55.440 --> 01:36:03.520 align:start position:0%
congregations, both non-hasidic andidic,
although notably, Kabad is not a member.

01:36:01.679 --> 01:36:10.080 align:start position:0%
Altogether among those who attend
synagogue in the US approximately 50%

01:36:06.560 --> 01:36:16.080 align:start position:0%
are reform around 30% are conservative
and 20% are orthodox. I should also

01:36:13.600 --> 01:36:20.960 align:start position:0%
point out reconstructionist or
reconstructing Judaism which can be

01:36:18.639 --> 01:36:27.040 align:start position:0%
considered a fourth branch of modern
Judaism founded by Morai Kaplan in the

01:36:24.320 --> 01:36:32.800 align:start position:0%
1950s. It can be seen as a breakaway
from conservative Judaism. However, like

01:36:30.080 --> 01:36:37.840 align:start position:0%
reformed Judaism, it does not see Jewish
law as being binding. But in contrast to

01:36:35.440 --> 01:36:43.040 align:start position:0%
reformed Judaism, it tends to place more
value on preserving old traditions and

01:36:40.239 --> 01:36:48.080 align:start position:0%
on maintaining a very distinct Jewish
identity. So you can kind of think of

01:36:45.360 --> 01:36:53.040 align:start position:0%
reconstructionist Judaism as being
somewhat conservative on the outside,

01:36:50.239 --> 01:36:58.320 align:start position:0%
but very liberal on the inside. There's
also renewal Judaism which is even more

01:36:56.159 --> 01:37:04.400 align:start position:0%
recent having its roots in the
countercultural movement of the 1960s

01:37:00.800 --> 01:37:10.960 align:start position:0%
and '7s. It too is a very liberal branch
of Judaism but tends to incorporate more

01:37:07.600 --> 01:37:16.080 align:start position:0%
mystical elements from hidic Judaism
which is why its followers are sometimes

01:37:13.119 --> 01:37:21.760 align:start position:0%
nicknamed hippie Jews. Now, one other
thing I should make clear is that in

01:37:18.800 --> 01:37:27.040 align:start position:0%
Judaism, denominational lines can be
quite blurry, especially in areas where

01:37:24.480 --> 01:37:32.800 align:start position:0%
there aren't many Jews. So, for example,
I live in Canada and when I converted to

01:37:30.080 --> 01:37:38.000 align:start position:0%
Judaism, I did so through a reform
synagogue, although one of the teachers

01:37:34.800 --> 01:37:43.440 align:start position:0%
was a reconstructionist. However, after
one year of study and the approval of a

01:37:40.320 --> 01:37:48.880 align:start position:0%
bait deen, I had a hatafat dambrit
performed by an Orthodox rabbi and was

01:37:46.400 --> 01:37:53.600 align:start position:0%
immersed in a mikvah at the Orthodox
synagogue. On top of this, the synagogue

01:37:51.600 --> 01:37:59.280 align:start position:0%
that my wife and I are most likely to
attend simply because it's the closest

01:37:55.760 --> 01:38:04.400 align:start position:0%
one to our home is actually renewal. So,
when people ask me which branch of

01:38:01.440 --> 01:38:09.440 align:start position:0%
Judaism I belong to, it's a difficult
question to answer. I usually just say

01:38:06.880 --> 01:38:14.000 align:start position:0%
that I'm a progressive Jew, which
basically encompasses everything other

01:38:11.679 --> 01:38:19.920 align:start position:0%
than Orthodox and in North America at
least is the dominant type of Judaism.

01:38:17.199 --> 01:38:25.679 align:start position:0%
But even between progressive Jews and
Orthodox Jews, there is often a lot of

01:38:22.960 --> 01:38:30.320 align:start position:0%
mixing. While each set of rabbis might
hold very different views, the actual

01:38:27.679 --> 01:38:35.840 align:start position:0%
members might not. So, it's not unusual
for a Jew with reformed leanings to

01:38:32.719 --> 01:38:40.400 align:start position:0%
attend an Orthodox synagogue or a fully
observant Orthodox Jew to attend a

01:38:38.560 --> 01:38:44.880 align:start position:0%
reformed synagogue. And then, of course,
there are sometimes separate safharti

01:38:42.800 --> 01:38:49.840 align:start position:0%
congregations. They usually see
themselves as being outside of the whole

01:38:47.760 --> 01:38:54.800 align:start position:0%
reform, conservative, Orthodox
dichotomy. But then there's also

01:38:52.159 --> 01:39:00.560 align:start position:0%
individual Sphartic Jews who do see
themselves as belonging to one of the

01:38:57.119 --> 01:39:06.400 align:start position:0%
three streams. So, it's complicated.
There are even humanist Jews who do not

01:39:03.920 --> 01:39:12.320 align:start position:0%
even believe in God, but still gather to
celebrate certain holidays or rights of

01:39:08.719 --> 01:39:16.800 align:start position:0%
passage. Now, what about Messianic Jews?
Well, Messianic Jews are really

01:39:14.239 --> 01:39:21.199 align:start position:0%
Christians. So, I actually talked about
them already on my series about

01:39:18.960 --> 01:39:26.480 align:start position:0%
Christian denominations. If you're
interested to hear my take on them, you

01:39:23.360 --> 01:39:31.600 align:start position:0%
can find it in episode 8. Okay, so that
was just how Judaism works in the US and

01:39:29.360 --> 01:39:36.960 align:start position:0%
maybe a few other countries like Canada
and the UK. In the UK, there are

01:39:33.840 --> 01:39:41.440 align:start position:0%
actually two major reform denominations,
liberal Judaism and the Movement for

01:39:39.360 --> 01:39:46.320 align:start position:0%
Reformed Judaism. However, quite
recently, in April of 2023, they

01:39:44.080 --> 01:39:51.840 align:start position:0%
announced their intention to merge into
a single organization. They also have a

01:39:49.199 --> 01:39:56.639 align:start position:0%
chief rabbi for their Orthodox Jews, who
you might have seen in the news recently

01:39:54.000 --> 01:40:03.199 align:start position:0%
as he participated in the coronation of
King Charles III. Let's now look at how

01:39:59.760 --> 01:40:07.760 align:start position:0%
Judaism works in Israel, which now has a
Jewish population that has surpassed

01:40:05.440 --> 01:40:12.880 align:start position:0%
that of the United States. Although
reform and conservative synagogues do

01:40:10.320 --> 01:40:18.639 align:start position:0%
exist in Israel in small numbers, the
reformed conservative orthodox tricotomy

01:40:15.520 --> 01:40:24.320 align:start position:0%
is far less important there. Instead, in
Israel, Jews are usually classified into

01:40:21.679 --> 01:40:30.080 align:start position:0%
four main categories. First, there are
the halon. These are secular Jews, and

01:40:27.520 --> 01:40:35.679 align:start position:0%
they actually make up a full half of all
the Jews in Israel. Next are the Mazorti

01:40:33.360 --> 01:40:40.960 align:start position:0%
who are traditional, meaning that they
are only partially observant. They make

01:40:38.400 --> 01:40:46.719 align:start position:0%
up another quarter of the Israeli
population. The final quarter consists

01:40:43.520 --> 01:40:51.840 align:start position:0%
of the Dati and Haredi. These are the
fully observant Jews with the Haredi,

01:40:49.440 --> 01:40:57.440 align:start position:0%
like I discussed earlier, being the most
strictly observant. Now, I'm not going

01:40:54.480 --> 01:41:03.199 align:start position:0%
to address Zionism in this video because
Zionism is more of a political thing

01:41:00.239 --> 01:41:07.920 align:start position:0%
than a religious thing. Individual Jews
across the world and across all

01:41:05.280 --> 01:41:12.239 align:start position:0%
denominations have differing views on
Zionism and the politics within Israel.

01:41:10.239 --> 01:41:16.000 align:start position:0%
So, it's important to remember that just
because someone is Jewish, that doesn't

01:41:14.239 --> 01:41:21.199 align:start position:0%
mean that they support every single
thing that the state of Israel does. But

01:41:19.040 --> 01:41:25.679 align:start position:0%
returning to the four categories of
Israeli Jews, I want to make it clear

01:41:23.360 --> 01:41:30.639 align:start position:0%
that these are not four different
denominations. For the most part,

01:41:27.840 --> 01:41:36.000 align:start position:0%
Israeli Jews are not really divided into
denominations at all. Instead, anything

01:41:33.360 --> 01:41:41.199 align:start position:0%
to do with Jewish religious matters in
Israel falls under the jurisdiction of

01:41:38.639 --> 01:41:46.880 align:start position:0%
the two chief rabbis, one of whom
represents Ashkanazi Jews and the other

01:41:43.600 --> 01:41:51.440 align:start position:0%
who represents Spharti Jews. This system
is actually the one that is used in most

01:41:49.440 --> 01:41:59.080 align:start position:0%
countries in the world. Some countries
such as France have just one chief rabbi

01:41:54.480 --> 01:42:01.100 align:start position:0%
whereas others like Argentina have two.
