01:42:01.360 --> 01:42:10.960 align:start position:0%
So obviously Christianity starts with
Jesus who lived from approximately 4

01:42:06.719 --> 01:42:15.280 align:start position:0%
B.CE to 30 CE. Since Jesus was a Jew,
most of his original followers were also

01:42:13.360 --> 01:42:19.760 align:start position:0%
Jews and they came from several
different branches of second temple

01:42:16.880 --> 01:42:25.280 align:start position:0%
Judaism. Originally those belonging to
the new movement started by Jesus were

01:42:22.480 --> 01:42:30.320 align:start position:0%
simply called the followers of the way.
But pretty soon more and more non-Jews

01:42:27.920 --> 01:42:34.960 align:start position:0%
started to join and thus the movement
eventually came to be seen as a

01:42:32.320 --> 01:42:39.600 align:start position:0%
completely new religion. Initially,
Christianity drew heavily from a group

01:42:37.040 --> 01:42:43.520 align:start position:0%
of people known as god-fearers. These
were Greeks and Romans who were

01:42:41.280 --> 01:42:48.719 align:start position:0%
attracted to Jewish ideas, but did not
want to fully convert to Judaism due to

01:42:46.320 --> 01:42:53.760 align:start position:0%
all of the various rules involved. Well,
Christianity had far fewer requirements.

01:42:51.520 --> 01:42:57.760 align:start position:0%
For example, no circumcision and no
dietary restrictions, and therefore, it

01:42:55.840 --> 01:43:02.080 align:start position:0%
was much easier for God-fearers to
convert to Christianity. So, many of

01:42:59.840 --> 01:43:07.280 align:start position:0%
them did. I should also point out that
while Christianity was mostly built upon

01:43:04.639 --> 01:43:12.400 align:start position:0%
Jewish ideas, it also inherited certain
ideas from Greek philosophy. Okay, so

01:43:10.560 --> 01:43:17.360 align:start position:0%
another important thing to know is that
in its early days, there was not really

01:43:14.560 --> 01:43:21.520 align:start position:0%
just one Christianity, but rather many
Christianities.

01:43:18.880 --> 01:43:26.719 align:start position:0%
From the perspective of the Christianity
that eventually became dominant, which

01:43:23.600 --> 01:43:31.199 align:start position:0%
I've labeled protoodox Christianity, all
of the other Christianities were

01:43:28.639 --> 01:43:35.760 align:start position:0%
heresies that had to be stamped out. One
of the big ones was Gnosticism, which

01:43:33.520 --> 01:43:41.760 align:start position:0%
eventually did die out, but ended up
influencing both Manakiism and Mandism.

01:43:39.760 --> 01:43:46.719 align:start position:0%
There were also the Ebianites and
Nazarines, who were mostly Jewish

01:43:44.159 --> 01:43:51.119 align:start position:0%
Christians who saw Jesus as the Messiah,
but not as God. They too died out but

01:43:49.360 --> 01:43:56.159 align:start position:0%
likely had an influence on the
development of Islam. The final

01:43:53.920 --> 01:44:01.280 align:start position:0%
alternative to what became the dominant
form of Christianity was Aryanism which

01:43:59.199 --> 01:44:06.400 align:start position:0%
taught that Jesus was a created being
who was elevated to the position of God.

01:44:04.320 --> 01:44:12.320 align:start position:0%
The controversy over this led to the
council of Nika in 325 in which Aryanism

01:44:10.000 --> 01:44:16.800 align:start position:0%
was rejected and the official set of
Christian beliefs was written down

01:44:14.320 --> 01:44:22.320 align:start position:0%
resulting in what is known today as the
Nyine creed. According to Nyine

01:44:19.760 --> 01:44:28.480 align:start position:0%
Christianity, Jesus and the father are
co-equal and co-eternal. Now a couple

01:44:25.440 --> 01:44:32.560 align:start position:0%
decades later in 380, Nyine Christianity
was made the official state religion of

01:44:30.480 --> 01:44:36.960 align:start position:0%
the Roman Empire. But you see by that
point there were also Christians outside

01:44:34.560 --> 01:44:42.480 align:start position:0%
of the Roman Empire particularly to the
east in the Sassinid Persian Empire.

01:44:40.159 --> 01:44:48.000 align:start position:0%
Thus around this time the church of the
east was established as a distinct

01:44:45.119 --> 01:44:51.920 align:start position:0%
group. From here the main church the one
that existed within the Roman Empire

01:44:49.920 --> 01:44:56.880 align:start position:0%
went on to be organized into five
pentarchies for administrative purposes.

01:44:55.199 --> 01:45:02.880 align:start position:0%
Basically this meant that there were
five main patriarchs each in a major

01:44:59.679 --> 01:45:07.840 align:start position:0%
city. Rome, Constantinople, Antioch,
which is in Syria, Jerusalem, and

01:45:05.520 --> 01:45:12.000 align:start position:0%
Alexandria, which is in Egypt. And the
thing is, there ended up being a bit of

01:45:09.760 --> 01:45:17.520 align:start position:0%
disagreement between these areas. In
Rome and Constantinople, an additional

01:45:14.639 --> 01:45:22.560 align:start position:0%
creed known as the Calcedonian Creed was
adopted and it clarified that although

01:45:20.080 --> 01:45:26.960 align:start position:0%
Jesus was equal to God, he had two
separate natures, one divine and one

01:45:24.800 --> 01:45:32.000 align:start position:0%
human. However, the other three
pentarchies did not accept this creed,

01:45:29.520 --> 01:45:36.639 align:start position:0%
arguing instead that Jesus had only one
nature, which was both divine and human

01:45:34.320 --> 01:45:40.719 align:start position:0%
at the same time. The division between
the Calcedonians and the

01:45:38.320 --> 01:45:45.040 align:start position:0%
non-caledonians, who became known as
oriental Orthodox, became even more

01:45:43.199 --> 01:45:50.239 align:start position:0%
distinct when all three of the
non-caledonian areas were taken over by

01:45:47.520 --> 01:45:55.199 align:start position:0%
Islam. Christianity continued to exist
in those areas, but was now in the

01:45:52.239 --> 01:46:01.520 align:start position:0%
minority. Today, the Syriak Orthodox
Church, the Coptic Orthodox Church in

01:45:57.760 --> 01:46:06.800 align:start position:0%
Egypt, and the Ethiopian Orthodox Tawah
Church all trace their roots to the

01:46:03.920 --> 01:46:11.600 align:start position:0%
three non-caledonian patriarchets from
the Roman era. In Rome and

01:46:09.440 --> 01:46:15.840 align:start position:0%
Constantinople, though, Christianity
continued to be the majority religion.

01:46:13.920 --> 01:46:20.639 align:start position:0%
And thus, it was these two cities that
continued to be the main centers of

01:46:18.239 --> 01:46:25.119 align:start position:0%
Christianity. For several more
centuries, Christianity in these two

01:46:22.800 --> 01:46:29.840 align:start position:0%
areas continued to be united, but
eventually they split. The area under

01:46:27.520 --> 01:46:34.400 align:start position:0%
Rome's jurisdiction became known as the
Catholic Church, and to this day, it is

01:46:32.400 --> 01:46:38.159 align:start position:0%
still led by the Patriarch of Rome,
although he's now better known as the

01:46:36.320 --> 01:46:42.800 align:start position:0%
Pope. Whereas the area under
Constantinople's jurisdiction became

01:46:40.480 --> 01:46:47.360 align:start position:0%
known as the Orthodox Church, still led
by the Patriarch of Constantinople.

01:46:45.440 --> 01:46:53.040 align:start position:0%
Today, the largest branch of the
Orthodox Church is actually the Russian

01:46:49.760 --> 01:46:57.199 align:start position:0%
Orthodox Church, which in 2018 cut ties
with Constantinople. Okay, for the rest

01:46:55.760 --> 01:47:02.080 align:start position:0%
of the chart, we'll be looking at the
many denominations that came about as a

01:46:59.520 --> 01:47:07.119 align:start position:0%
result of the Protestant Reformation. It
started in 1517 as a reform movement

01:47:05.199 --> 01:47:11.360 align:start position:0%
within the Catholic Church, but quickly
led to the creation of three new

01:47:08.880 --> 01:47:16.320 align:start position:0%
branches of Christianity, mostly along
state lines. Lutheranism based on the

01:47:14.239 --> 01:47:22.000 align:start position:0%
teachings of Martin Luther became
dominant in many German states as well

01:47:18.960 --> 01:47:26.480 align:start position:0%
as in Scandinavia. Calvinism based on
the teachings of John Calvin became

01:47:24.159 --> 01:47:31.679 align:start position:0%
dominant in the Dutch Republic and
Scotland. And finally, Anglicanism

01:47:29.119 --> 01:47:36.159 align:start position:0%
became dominant in England. Take note
that the Calvinist branch is also known

01:47:34.080 --> 01:47:39.760 align:start position:0%
as the reformed branch and that
Calvinist churches that trace their

01:47:37.840 --> 01:47:43.920 align:start position:0%
roots to Scotland are known as
Presbyterians.

01:47:41.440 --> 01:47:48.719 align:start position:0%
Now, there was also a fourth Protestant
movement early on that was even more

01:47:46.239 --> 01:47:53.679 align:start position:0%
radical. Its followers became known as
Anabaptists because they taught that

01:47:51.040 --> 01:47:58.000 align:start position:0%
adults should be rebaptized. Groups that
trace their roots to this movement

01:47:55.360 --> 01:48:01.840 align:start position:0%
include the Brethren, the Menanites, and
the Amish. Okay. From here on out, we'll

01:48:00.800 --> 01:48:05.520 align:start position:0%
mostly be dealing with the
English-speaking world, at first, Great

01:48:04.080 --> 01:48:10.239 align:start position:0%
Britain, and then mostly [clears throat]
the United States. Since Anglicanism

01:48:08.400 --> 01:48:14.960 align:start position:0%
continued to operate a lot like
Catholicism, meaning that it had a very

01:48:12.400 --> 01:48:19.199 align:start position:0%
top- down structure, a bunch of smaller,
more loosely organized church groups

01:48:17.040 --> 01:48:22.719 align:start position:0%
eventually started to pop up as well.
Collectively, the people belonging to

01:48:20.960 --> 01:48:26.639 align:start position:0%
these groups were known as English
separatists, and many of them ended up

01:48:24.960 --> 01:48:30.880 align:start position:0%
traveling to the Americas where they
could have more religious freedom.

01:48:28.560 --> 01:48:34.800 align:start position:0%
However, most of the original groups,
such as the Puritans, eventually fizzled

01:48:33.040 --> 01:48:39.360 align:start position:0%
out. But two that didn't were the
Quakers and the Baptists. We'll be

01:48:37.360 --> 01:48:43.760 align:start position:0%
coming back to the Baptists in a moment,
but for now, take note that there were

01:48:41.440 --> 01:48:48.159 align:start position:0%
also many congregations that simply
