01:51:21.600 --> 01:51:28.560 align:start position:0%
different denominations. The term
denomination itself might not apply here

01:51:26.159 --> 01:51:32.320 align:start position:0%
very accurately. Let's get into it and
I'll explain along the way. The first

01:51:30.719 --> 01:51:37.280 align:start position:0%
thing I would like to address is that
most religions have multiple stories of

01:51:34.719 --> 01:51:42.639 align:start position:0%
their origins. Typically, there's one or
more traditional accounts along with one

01:51:39.760 --> 01:51:46.800 align:start position:0%
or more academic accounts. For example,
as Matt mentioned in his video on

01:51:44.880 --> 01:51:51.280 align:start position:0%
Judaism, while Jews believe their
religion to have begun when Moses

01:51:48.800 --> 01:51:56.000 align:start position:0%
received the Torah, academic scholars
believe it to have emerged out of a mix

01:51:53.679 --> 01:52:01.360 align:start position:0%
of ancient Israelite, Egyptian, and
Mesopotamian religions. Similarly for

01:51:59.040 --> 01:52:06.080 align:start position:0%
Islam there's a traditional account that
states that Islam began with Adam the

01:52:03.840 --> 01:52:12.320 align:start position:0%
first human and subsequent prophets
which include Noah, Moses and Jesus

01:52:09.040 --> 01:52:16.880 align:start position:0%
preached Islam but in a different form.
Finally it came into its current shape

01:52:14.719 --> 01:52:22.560 align:start position:0%
with prophet Muhammad when he received
the first revelation of the Quran in 610

01:52:19.599 --> 01:52:26.880 align:start position:0%
CE or so. However, academic scholars
believe that Islam came out of the

01:52:24.639 --> 01:52:31.520 align:start position:0%
mixing of various religions which
included the ancient Arabic pagan

01:52:29.520 --> 01:52:36.080 align:start position:0%
religious traditions and a group of
people known as Jewish Christians,

01:52:33.920 --> 01:52:42.800 align:start position:0%
specifically the Ebianites and the
Nazarenes who upheld the laws of Judaism

01:52:39.360 --> 01:52:47.119 align:start position:0%
but also believed Jesus to be a Messiah.
They may have fled into Arabia to avoid

01:52:45.119 --> 01:52:51.679 align:start position:0%
persecution where they inspired the
religion of Islam. Islamic tradition

01:52:49.520 --> 01:52:57.520 align:start position:0%
mentions a group of people known as
Hanife who followed the quote true

01:52:54.560 --> 01:53:02.880 align:start position:0%
monotheism of prophet Abraham which may
or may not have been these Jewish

01:52:59.840 --> 01:53:06.560 align:start position:0%
Christians. Anyhow, according to Islamic
tradition, Islam began with the

01:53:04.560 --> 01:53:13.119 align:start position:0%
revelation of the Quran to the prophet
Muhammad around 610 CE. From then to his

01:53:10.080 --> 01:53:18.000 align:start position:0%
death around 632, the prophet continued
to receive revelations from Allah, the

01:53:15.679 --> 01:53:24.400 align:start position:0%
Arabic word for God, which were later
compiled into a book format known as the

01:53:20.719 --> 01:53:29.840 align:start position:0%
Quran or recitation. The Quran forms the
core of Islam and is universally held up

01:53:27.119 --> 01:53:34.639 align:start position:0%
by Muslims as the highest authority on
their religion. They might disagree on

01:53:32.320 --> 01:53:41.599 align:start position:0%
interpretations of the Quran, but all
Muslims hold it up above everything

01:53:37.199 --> 01:53:46.880 align:start position:0%
else. In 622 around 11 or 12 years after
the first revelation, the prophet went

01:53:43.679 --> 01:53:51.679 align:start position:0%
into exile from his birth city of Mecca
and formed a community in a city called

01:53:49.280 --> 01:53:56.960 align:start position:0%
Yatre, which later came to be known as
Medina. This immigration of the prophet

01:53:54.320 --> 01:54:01.599 align:start position:0%
is known as Tahra and is considered a
very important point in the history of

01:53:58.800 --> 01:54:06.560 align:start position:0%
Islam. So much so that this year marks
the beginning of the Islamic lunar

01:54:03.760 --> 01:54:13.760 align:start position:0%
calendar. It also marks a changing point
in the Quran. The Quran is divided into

01:54:10.000 --> 01:54:18.000 align:start position:0%
114 chapters known as the suras. The
Meccan chapters which were revealed

01:54:15.679 --> 01:54:23.040 align:start position:0%
during the prophet's time in Mecca focus
more on for the lack of better term

01:54:20.159 --> 01:54:28.880 align:start position:0%
abstract concepts. To generalize, the
Quran talks about things such as or

01:54:26.239 --> 01:54:33.520 align:start position:0%
monotheism, the oneness of God, the day
of judgment or as it's called in the

01:54:30.880 --> 01:54:38.159 align:start position:0%
Quran, the hour when the world will end
and humanity will be resurrected to face

01:54:36.000 --> 01:54:43.440 align:start position:0%
the final judgment. for where they'd
spend eternity, heaven or hell. In other

01:54:41.119 --> 01:54:49.199 align:start position:0%
words, these chapters focused on
theology. However, after the hijra, the

01:54:46.400 --> 01:54:54.159 align:start position:0%
Quran started talking more about, again,
for the lack of a better term, matters

01:54:51.280 --> 01:54:58.880 align:start position:0%
of the world. Because in Medina, the
prophet wasn't just a prophet. He was

01:54:56.800 --> 01:55:04.320 align:start position:0%
also a political leader. So, he had to
arbitrate over disputes, go to war, do

01:55:01.520 --> 01:55:09.760 align:start position:0%
diplomacy, etc. So the Quran also
focuses on such matters at this point.

01:55:07.119 --> 01:55:15.119 align:start position:0%
In other words, these chapters focused
on Jewish prudence or law. This is

01:55:12.800 --> 01:55:20.719 align:start position:0%
important because in Islam there are two
important distinctions when it comes to

01:55:17.440 --> 01:55:26.080 align:start position:0%
what one believes. The first is your
which deals with the theological nature

01:55:22.960 --> 01:55:31.280 align:start position:0%
of Islam while the second the deals with
the judicial nature of Islam. Where the

01:55:28.719 --> 01:55:36.719 align:start position:0%
fik deals with what to do with lawb
breakakers, the akida deals with why

01:55:33.920 --> 01:55:41.360 align:start position:0%
someone becomes one. Where the fik would
say that the punishment for someone who

01:55:38.560 --> 01:55:46.880 align:start position:0%
commits a particular sin is this or
that. The would ask whether the sinner

01:55:44.239 --> 01:55:54.400 align:start position:0%
has free will or whether everything is
predestined. These two do overlap and

01:55:50.000 --> 01:55:59.599 align:start position:0%
the does guide the but not always. The
prophet Muhammad passed away in 632 and

01:55:57.199 --> 01:56:04.000 align:start position:0%
immediately Kra began appearing in the
community of the believers. The first

01:56:01.760 --> 01:56:08.239 align:start position:0%
point of disagreement was who would lead
the community as its new political

01:56:06.080 --> 01:56:13.520 align:start position:0%
leader. Some senior followers of the
prophet elected his close friend Abu

01:56:10.320 --> 01:56:19.199 align:start position:0%
Bakr as the first khalifa or kaiff.
Kaiff simply means successor or deputy.

01:56:16.719 --> 01:56:24.719 align:start position:0%
The kiff was to be the new political
leader of the believers and was known as

01:56:21.679 --> 01:56:29.760 align:start position:0%
Amir Alminin or literally the leader of
the believers. However, another party of

01:56:27.599 --> 01:56:34.239 align:start position:0%
the followers of the prophet wanted Ali
Iban Abi Talib, the cousin and

01:56:31.760 --> 01:56:38.800 align:start position:0%
son-in-law of the prophet to succeed him
as Kaiff. It's tempting to call this

01:56:36.639 --> 01:56:43.360 align:start position:0%
decision as having laid the foundation
of the division between the Sunnis and

01:56:40.880 --> 01:56:48.239 align:start position:0%
the Shia, the two largest sects of
Islam. However, these two sects wouldn't

01:56:46.320 --> 01:56:52.159 align:start position:0%
really crystallize till the 11th
century. So, it would be better to call

01:56:50.000 --> 01:56:57.199 align:start position:0%
these two groups protoshia and
protosnis. The division is often

01:56:54.800 --> 01:57:01.440 align:start position:0%
oversimplified by saying that the proto
Sunnis were the ones who supported Abu

01:56:59.119 --> 01:57:06.880 align:start position:0%
Bakr while the protoshia were the ones
who supported Ali. Initially, this was

01:57:04.159 --> 01:57:11.440 align:start position:0%
the case. The division was merely about
who would lead the community. However,

01:57:09.199 --> 01:57:17.520 align:start position:0%
over time, the division began to get
more and more complex. This was because

01:57:14.560 --> 01:57:21.520 align:start position:0%
the community expanded really quickly.
During the prophet's lifetime, he

01:57:19.360 --> 01:57:26.560 align:start position:0%
conquered and allied with much of the
Arabian Peninsula. After him, the caiffs

01:57:24.560 --> 01:57:30.960 align:start position:0%
sent their armies into the greater
Middle East. Within a few decades, the

01:57:29.040 --> 01:57:36.239 align:start position:0%
believers ruled everything between
Tunisia and India. In the process, they

01:57:33.920 --> 01:57:42.080 align:start position:0%
defeated the Byzantine and the Sassined
Empires. As you might expect, this huge

01:57:39.040 --> 01:57:46.880 align:start position:0%
empire brought its own problems. The
kaiffs had to make judgments and

01:57:44.400 --> 01:57:52.159 align:start position:0%
policies in political, social, and
military matters. The believers tried to

01:57:49.520 --> 01:57:57.280 align:start position:0%
follow the law laid down in the Quran as
it was and is the highest authority with

01:57:55.280 --> 01:58:02.159 align:start position:0%
things that weren't directly addressed
in the Quran. The believers looked at

01:57:59.679 --> 01:58:07.040 align:start position:0%
the examples laid down by the prophet in
his lifetime. These examples along with

01:58:04.800 --> 01:58:11.599 align:start position:0%
his sayings formed a cannon of the
Islamic tradition known as the Sunnah of

01:58:09.440 --> 01:58:16.400 align:start position:0%
the prophet. However, there were still
many many things that had no direct

01:58:14.000 --> 01:58:22.080 align:start position:0%
parallels in the Quran or the Sunnah.
How do we resolve that? This question

01:58:19.040 --> 01:58:27.119 align:start position:0%
divided the Muslims further. Let's first
look at how the Sunnis answered this

01:58:24.000 --> 01:58:31.599 align:start position:0%
question. Again to grossly oversimplify,
the proto Sunnis who get their name from

01:58:29.440 --> 01:58:36.159 align:start position:0%
the Sunnah believed that the examples of
the prophet can guide the believers

01:58:33.840 --> 01:58:41.520 align:start position:0%
along with the opinions and comments of
learned men and occasionally women who

01:58:38.800 --> 01:58:46.400 align:start position:0%
came to be known as the ama and who had
spent considerable portions of their

01:58:43.520 --> 01:58:52.400 align:start position:0%
lives studying the Quran and the Sunnah.
The ama weren't exactly priests, but

01:58:49.440 --> 01:58:57.280 align:start position:0%
they were not that dissimilar to rabbis.
In fact, a lot of Islamic Jewish

01:58:54.080 --> 01:59:02.000 align:start position:0%
prudence has parallels with Jewish law.
Anyhow, among the Ola, there were some

01:58:59.840 --> 01:59:07.920 align:start position:0%
distinguished figures who are more
venerated than the others who came to be

01:59:04.719 --> 01:59:12.159 align:start position:0%
known as the imams. While Sunni imams
were respectable figures who were

01:59:09.920 --> 01:59:17.199 align:start position:0%
considered authorities on the subject of
Jewish prudence, they weren't infallible

01:59:14.800 --> 01:59:23.360 align:start position:0%
and they were merely educated human
beings. However, the protoshia believed

01:59:20.480 --> 01:59:26.960 align:start position:0%
that their imams were infallible. They
believed that the Imam has to be a

01:59:25.280 --> 01:59:32.239 align:start position:0%
descendant of the prophet through his
daughter Fatima and her husband Ali Iban

01:59:29.520 --> 01:59:37.520 align:start position:0%
Abu Talib. The protoshia believed that
the Imam had divine guidance and was the

01:59:35.119 --> 01:59:42.639 align:start position:0%
sole authority on how to interpret the
Quran and the traditions of the prophet.

01:59:40.320 --> 01:59:47.040 align:start position:0%
Ali Iban Abi Talib is considered the
first Imam and then his two sons

01:59:44.800 --> 01:59:52.080 align:start position:0%
Al-Hassan and Al Hussein are considered
the second and third respectively. The

01:59:49.840 --> 01:59:56.639 align:start position:0%
disagreement over imams and their role
in Islamic society is perhaps the

01:59:54.560 --> 02:00:01.679 align:start position:0%
biggest distinction between the Sunnis
and the Shia even today. Both have their

01:59:59.440 --> 02:00:05.760 align:start position:0%
own chains of imams who are considered
founders of their various schools of

02:00:03.840 --> 02:00:10.719 align:start position:0%
Islamic Jewish prudence and developed
their own interpretations of Islamic law

02:00:08.159 --> 02:00:15.440 align:start position:0%
known as the Sharia. However, it must be
kept in mind that back in the day, this

02:00:12.880 --> 02:00:20.960 align:start position:0%
wasn't a binary division. Rather, it was
more of a spectrum where people could

02:00:17.679 --> 02:00:26.080 align:start position:0%
and did mix elements from both. Let's
look at Sunnis first. Sunnis make up

02:00:23.599 --> 02:00:32.000 align:start position:0%
roughly 90% of the Muslim population
with roughly 9% being Shia and the rest

02:00:29.040 --> 02:00:37.119 align:start position:0%
making up less than 1%. Among the
Sunnis, there are four schools of Jerus

02:00:34.080 --> 02:00:42.239 align:start position:0%
Prunes or Fik. These are the hanafi
which is the largest and is most popular

02:00:39.360 --> 02:00:47.520 align:start position:0%
in India, Pakistan, Turkey and parts of
the Middle East. The Maliki which is

02:00:44.880 --> 02:00:53.599 align:start position:0%
popular in Africa and previously was the
predominant school in Muslim Spain. Then

02:00:50.480 --> 02:00:57.920 align:start position:0%
the Shafi and Humbli both of which are
mostly common in the Middle East with

02:00:55.679 --> 02:01:02.960 align:start position:0%
the Humbali being dominant in Saudi
Arabia. There used to be a fifth one

02:01:00.400 --> 02:01:07.840 align:start position:0%
named Zahiri which was popular in Muslim
Spain and northwestern Africa but it has

02:01:05.599 --> 02:01:11.840 align:start position:0%
since died out but recently with the
Islamic revivalist movements it is

02:01:10.000 --> 02:01:16.800 align:start position:0%
starting to make a comeback. We'll talk
about that in a moment. Now early on in

02:01:14.480 --> 02:01:21.599 align:start position:0%
its life Islam came into contact with
the Greeks and their way of thinking. So

02:01:19.599 --> 02:01:26.400 align:start position:0%
there was a debate in the Islamic world
about what way of thinking should be

02:01:23.760 --> 02:01:31.360 align:start position:0%
followed. Should we adhere rigidly to
the Quran and the Sunnah or should a

02:01:28.719 --> 02:01:36.639 align:start position:0%
logical approach to rational thinking be
developed for our worldly problems? This

02:01:34.480 --> 02:01:42.000 align:start position:0%
led to the creation of the schools of
theology. The Aari are considered the

02:01:39.520 --> 02:01:47.440 align:start position:0%
traditionalists who stick to the Quran
and Sunnah while the muzzelites are seen

02:01:44.639 --> 02:01:52.719 align:start position:0%
as those who follow reason and rational
thinking much more. The Ashari and the

02:01:50.239 --> 02:01:56.960 align:start position:0%
Matidi are somewhere in between.
Although the division between these

02:01:54.159 --> 02:02:01.679 align:start position:0%
schools which are quite clear in theory
weren't as neat in practice. For

02:01:59.199 --> 02:02:05.920 align:start position:0%
example, the Melites while claiming to
be rationalists and progressive were

02:02:04.000 --> 02:02:10.719 align:start position:0%
behind one of the biggest inquisitions
in Islamic history. This inquisition

02:02:08.400 --> 02:02:15.679 align:start position:0%
also stopped Islam from having something
of a pope. A little bit about that

02:02:13.040 --> 02:02:20.000 align:start position:0%
inquisition which is called the Mina. It
was during the reign of Abassad Kaiff

02:02:17.760 --> 02:02:24.239 align:start position:0%
al- Mammoon. The main question was about
the nature of the Quran. Whether it was

02:02:22.080 --> 02:02:29.280 align:start position:0%
created at the time of revelation to the
prophet or whether it had always

02:02:26.639 --> 02:02:34.080 align:start position:0%
existed. The implications of that were
that if the Quran had always existed

02:02:31.920 --> 02:02:38.480 align:start position:0%
since the beginning of time, then it is
true for all times and its

02:02:36.080 --> 02:02:43.520 align:start position:0%
interpretations cannot change or be
updated over time. However, if it was

02:02:41.599 --> 02:02:49.280 align:start position:0%
created at the time of revelation that
it meant that the Quran applied only to

02:02:46.080 --> 02:02:54.400 align:start position:0%
that time and its meaning can be changed
according to the times. Al-Mamoon

02:02:51.920 --> 02:02:59.440 align:start position:0%
believed in himself as being the Imam
and having the power to define Islamic

02:02:56.880 --> 02:03:05.520 align:start position:0%
theology and Jewish prudence rather than
the body of learned men and women known

02:03:02.159 --> 02:03:10.239 align:start position:0%
as the Ola. The Moazelites supported him
while the most ardent opponent was Imam

02:03:08.000 --> 02:03:15.119 align:start position:0%
Ahmed Iban Hal, the founder of the
Humbali school. People were forced to

02:03:12.880 --> 02:03:20.000 align:start position:0%
support Al-Mamoon's doctrine of the
created Quran and refusal led to

02:03:17.760 --> 02:03:25.440 align:start position:0%
imprisonment, torture, seizure of
property, etc. When the Inquisition

02:03:22.639 --> 02:03:29.520 align:start position:0%
failed, the Mozelites fell into decline
and eventually died out. But recently

02:03:28.000 --> 02:03:34.560 align:start position:0%
people have been claiming to be
neomotoites and trying to revive the

02:03:32.400 --> 02:03:39.360 align:start position:0%
rationalist thinking that is often
imagined as being the core of their

02:03:36.719 --> 02:03:44.480 align:start position:0%
doctrine. Since the Mahna failed, Sunni
kiffs never again tried to have the

02:03:41.840 --> 02:03:49.199 align:start position:0%
power to define Islamic theology and
Jewish prudence directly. This is why

02:03:46.719 --> 02:03:53.360 align:start position:0%
Sunni Islam has no head of faith like
the pope. Over time, the schools of

02:03:51.599 --> 02:03:58.080 align:start position:0%
theology and the schools of Jewish
prudence came to be associated with each

02:03:55.599 --> 02:04:02.639 align:start position:0%
other. For example, the humblies follow
the author school while the hanafi

02:04:00.159 --> 02:04:06.719 align:start position:0%
follow the maturi one. The humblies
stick to a more literal meaning of the

02:04:04.560 --> 02:04:11.040 align:start position:0%
Quran and sunnah while the hanafies
being a centrist school do use some

02:04:08.960 --> 02:04:17.040 align:start position:0%
rational thinking as well along with
analogy and consensus to form judgments.

02:04:14.480 --> 02:04:22.480 align:start position:0%
However, for most Muslims today, their
school of theology aren't very clear.

02:04:20.080 --> 02:04:26.800 align:start position:0%
They usually identify with the mudhub or
school of juristprudence more than the

02:04:24.320 --> 02:04:31.599 align:start position:0%
school of theology. In fact, even
mosques can be named after the mudhub of

02:04:29.280 --> 02:04:35.760 align:start position:0%
the people who manage them. Usually in
Muslim majority countries, people tend

02:04:33.760 --> 02:04:40.800 align:start position:0%
to go to the mosque that is managed by
the people of their own mub because

02:04:38.159 --> 02:04:46.159 align:start position:0%
mosques are primarily used for prayers
and the way to pray also changes from

02:04:43.440 --> 02:04:51.119 align:start position:0%
math to mhab. However, in western
countries, people go to whatever mosque

02:04:48.400 --> 02:04:56.320 align:start position:0%
is available as long as it follows their
sect, i.e. the Sunni one or the Shia

02:04:53.760 --> 02:05:01.040 align:start position:0%
one. In the 18th century, the Muslim
world began to lose much of its power as

02:04:58.719 --> 02:05:05.679 align:start position:0%
the Ottoman and Mughal empires entered
an era of decline and the Europeans

02:05:03.440 --> 02:05:10.800 align:start position:0%
began to take over. At this point,
Muslims faced the question of why this

02:05:08.239 --> 02:05:15.920 align:start position:0%
had happened. Many scholars came to the
conclusion that Muslims had slid away

02:05:13.119 --> 02:05:21.040 align:start position:0%
from true Islam and had become sinful
which led to this decline. As a result,

02:05:18.800 --> 02:05:26.400 align:start position:0%
many revivalist movements appeared in
the Islamic world. The first one came

02:05:23.440 --> 02:05:31.599 align:start position:0%
from India under a man named Shahalu
Dehelvi in the early and mid 18th

02:05:29.040 --> 02:05:36.000 align:start position:0%
century. He advocated for Muslims to
stop following medieval imams such as

02:05:34.080 --> 02:05:41.360 align:start position:0%
the founders of the four mhabs and
instead focus on learning for themselves

02:05:38.400 --> 02:05:46.560 align:start position:0%
what the Quran and the Sunnah teach. He
and his son even translated the Quran

02:05:43.840 --> 02:05:51.119 align:start position:0%
into Persian and Udu respectively which
were the two dominant languages among

02:05:48.800 --> 02:05:56.159 align:start position:0%
Indian Muslims at the time to make the
Quran more accessible to the people.

02:05:54.000 --> 02:06:00.880 align:start position:0%
Towards the end of the 18th century,
another reformer was active in what is

02:05:58.480 --> 02:06:06.000 align:start position:0%
today Saudi Arabia. His name was
Muhammad Iban Abdul Wahab. He also

02:06:03.599 --> 02:06:10.639 align:start position:0%
advocated for a similar disassociation
with the medieval imams and their

02:06:08.000 --> 02:06:15.040 align:start position:0%
schools and for re-evaluating the Quran
and Sunnah. Over time, his doctrine

02:06:13.040 --> 02:06:20.719 align:start position:0%
known as Wahhabism came to become
dominant in Saudi Arabia. Wahhabis are

02:06:17.840 --> 02:06:24.719 align:start position:0%
often put in the same box as the aadith
who were born in India. The two

02:06:22.800 --> 02:06:30.159 align:start position:0%
movements might have even inspired each
other. They're both

02:06:27.520 --> 02:06:35.440 align:start position:0%
meaning they claim to not adhere to any
medieval school, but in fact they do

02:06:32.960 --> 02:06:40.880 align:start position:0%
kind of adhere to the humbly one. They
call themselves Salafi after the Salafi

02:06:38.159 --> 02:06:46.079 align:start position:0%
movement which advocated for a return of
Muslims to the ways of the Aslaf or the

02:06:43.520 --> 02:06:51.440 align:start position:0%
elders meaning the first generation of
Muslims. The Wahhabis are a bit more

02:06:48.960 --> 02:06:56.239 align:start position:0%
fundamentalist if you will while the Ali
hadith are a bit more moderate. The Ali

02:06:54.560 --> 02:07:01.679 align:start position:0%
Hadith came from the followers of
Shavealula along with the Bundis who

02:06:58.800 --> 02:07:07.040 align:start position:0%
follow Shaalula but also adhere to the
Hanafi Mhub. They along with the Bilv

02:07:04.800 --> 02:07:13.840 align:start position:0%
are the majority of the Muslims in India
and Pakistan. The Bilv are kind of

02:07:10.400 --> 02:07:19.440 align:start position:0%
Hanafi mixed with a lot of Sufism. So
while the ah hadith, the Wahhabis and

02:07:16.320 --> 02:07:24.079 align:start position:0%
the Obandis don't like Sufism, the Bilvs
do quite a lot actually. Speaking of the

02:07:22.400 --> 02:07:29.119 align:start position:0%
Sufis, we're not going to be talking
about them in detail here because

02:07:26.239 --> 02:07:33.280 align:start position:0%
they're very complicated. Sufism is a
mystical form of Islam and they have

02:07:31.199 --> 02:07:38.480 align:start position:0%
many orders and brotherhoods that
believe in a range of religious

02:07:35.119 --> 02:07:43.920 align:start position:0%
traditions. Some are strictly Shia, some
